        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Algorithmic Arts, Media Studies, and Interdisciplinary Creativity (JAAMIC) is an international, peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing original research that explores the intersections of computation, creativity, media, and culture. The journal provides a multidisciplinary platform for advancing critical, theoretical, and practice-based knowledge on how algorithms, digital media, and emerging technologies are transforming artistic practices, communication systems, and interdisciplinary innovation.</p>\n<h4>Aims</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal aims to:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Promote high-quality research on algorithmic and computational approaches to the arts, humanities, and media.</li><li>Encourage interdisciplinary dialogue between media studies, computer science, digital humanities, design, and creative industries.</li><li>Provide a critical forum for examining the social, ethical, cultural, and philosophical implications of algorithm-driven creativity.</li><li>Support innovative methodologies combining theoretical research with experimental, practice-based, and applied perspectives.</li><li>Foster global contributions by welcoming diverse cultural, disciplinary, and regional perspectives on digital creativity.</li></ul>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JAAMIC invites submissions of original research articles, reviews, essays, and practice-based studies in the following broad subject areas:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Algorithmic Arts &amp; Digital Creativity: generative and computational art, AI-based creativity, machine learning in artistic practices, digital aesthetics, and interactive media.</li><li>Media Studies &amp; Communication: digital platforms, cultural and media theory, transmedia storytelling, film and visual studies, video games, and immersive/extended reality (XR).</li><li>Humanities &amp; Critical Inquiry: critical algorithm studies, philosophy of technology, posthumanism, semiotics, digital ethics, and cultural theory.</li><li>Creative and Interdisciplinary Practices: sound and music technologies, creative coding, digital performance, data visualization, hybrid practices, and digital pedagogy.</li><li>Policy, Society &amp; Ethics: copyright and intellectual property in digital arts, algorithmic bias and accountability, diversity and inclusion, sustainability, and global creative economies.</li></ul>\n<h4>Readership</h4>\n<p>The journal is intended for academics, researchers, artists, designers, media practitioners, technologists, and policymakers engaged in the study of algorithms, media, and interdisciplinary creativity.</p>\n<p>By combining rigorous scholarly inquiry with openness to creative experimentation, JAAMIC seeks to establish itself as a leading international reference for advancing debates on digital culture, algorithmic practices, and cross-disciplinary innovation.</p>",
