        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Cultural Anthropology, Visual Culture, and Societal Imagination (JCAVCSI) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on human societies, cultural practices, and visual expression. JCAVCSI provides a platform for critical, empirical, and theoretical research that explores the ways culture, imagery, and collective imagination shape human experience, social structures, and societal transformation.</p>\n<p>The journal aims to foster understanding of cultural dynamics through the lens of anthropology, visual studies, and societal imagination, emphasizing the interplay between tradition, innovation, and representation. It encourages contributions that examine both the theoretical frameworks and practical manifestations of culture, including art, media, ritual, and everyday practices, across diverse societies and historical contexts.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JCAVCSI welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case studies, critical reviews, and practice-based scholarship across a broad range of subject areas, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Cultural Anthropology:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Ethnography, field studies, and comparative cultural analysis</li><li>Social organization, identity, and cultural practices</li><li>Rituals, customs, and intangible cultural heritage</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Visual Culture:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Art, media, film, photography, and digital visual practices</li><li>Visual storytelling, representation, and cultural imagery</li><li>Intersection of visual culture with identity, memory, and politics</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Societal Imagination and Cultural Theory:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Collective imagination, myth, and narrative in society</li><li>Cultural memory, heritage, and symbolic practices</li><li>Critical theory, postcolonial studies, and interdisciplinary perspectives</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of anthropology, sociology, media studies, art history, and cultural studies</li><li>Digital humanities, ethnomusicology, and performance studies</li><li>Innovative methodologies bridging qualitative, quantitative, and practice-led research</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Transformative Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Community-based cultural initiatives and participatory research</li><li>Policy, governance, and ethics in cultural preservation</li><li>Creative and practice-oriented approaches to understanding society</li></ul>\n<p>JCAVCSI serves as a platform for scholars, practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the complex relationships between culture, visual representation, and societal imagination. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, encourages critical dialogue, and contributes to the understanding of cultural dynamics, human creativity, and social transformation.</p>",
