        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Film, Television, and Popular Culture (JFTPC) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing scholarship on visual media, entertainment, and cultural phenomena. JFTPC provides a rigorous platform for critical, theoretical, and empirical research examining the intersections of film, television, and popular culture in shaping social values, cultural identity, and collective imagination.</p>\n<p>The journal aims to explore the cultural, social, political, and technological dimensions of media production and consumption, highlighting how storytelling and popular narratives influence and reflect human experience across historical and contemporary contexts. It encourages interdisciplinary approaches, integrating insights from media studies, cultural studies, sociology, communication, and the arts.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JFTPC welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, critical reviews, and practice-based scholarship across a wide range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Film Studies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Cinema history, theory, and criticism</li><li>Genre studies, auteur theory, and narrative analysis</li><li>National and transnational cinema, independent and mainstream film</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Television Studies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Television history, programming, and audience studies</li><li>Reality TV, streaming platforms, and digital series</li><li>Representation, ideology, and cultural influence in televised media</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Popular Culture:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Media, fandom, and subcultures</li><li>Music, fashion, gaming, and digital entertainment</li><li>Social media, meme culture, and participatory cultural practices</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Perspectives:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Media sociology, cultural theory, and communication studies</li><li>Political, ethical, and economic dimensions of media production</li><li>Digital humanities, media technology, and visual culture studies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Practice-Led Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Media pedagogy, production studies, and creative practice</li><li>Media activism, social change, and audience engagement</li><li>Innovative methodologies in media and cultural research</li></ul>\n<p>JFTPC serves as a dynamic platform for scholars, media practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to examine the impact of film, television, and popular culture on society. The journal emphasizes work that bridges theory and practice, fosters critical dialogue, and contributes to a deeper understanding of media, culture, and collective imagination in a rapidly evolving digital landscape.</p>",
