        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Food, Culture, and Anthropology (JFCA) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to exploring the complex relationships between food, culture, society, and human behavior. The journal provides a platform for interdisciplinary scholarship that examines how food practices, culinary traditions, and consumption patterns shape cultural identity, social structures, and community life across diverse contexts.</p>\n<p>JFCA aims to advance research on the cultural, social, historical, and anthropological dimensions of food, emphasizing the ways in which food practices intersect with rituals, heritage, globalization, sustainability, and everyday life. The journal encourages contributions that integrate theoretical analysis, ethnographic study, and applied research, fostering a deeper understanding of food as both a cultural and anthropological phenomenon.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JFCA welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, ethnographic reports, critical reviews, and practice-based scholarship across a wide range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Food and Cultural Practices:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Culinary traditions, regional and indigenous cuisines</li><li>Rituals, festivals, and symbolic uses of food</li><li>Foodways as markers of identity, community, and heritage</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Anthropological and Sociological Perspectives:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Food and social structures, kinship, and community networks</li><li>Cross-cultural studies of consumption patterns and dietary norms</li><li>Globalization, migration, and food-related cultural transformations</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Food, Health, and Sustainability:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Traditional and contemporary food systems</li><li>Nutritional anthropology and cultural implications of diets</li><li>Sustainable, ethical, and locally informed food practices</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of anthropology, cultural studies, sociology, and history</li><li>Food in media, literature, and visual culture</li><li>Digital and participatory methodologies in food research</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Public Engagement:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Food heritage preservation and cultural policy</li><li>Community-based and participatory food research</li><li>Culinary education, tourism, and heritage promotion</li></ul>\n<p>JFCA serves as a platform for scholars, practitioners, and researchers to investigate the multifaceted roles of food in human life. The journal emphasizes work that bridges theory and practice, fosters interdisciplinary dialogue, and contributes to a comprehensive understanding of the cultural, social, and anthropological significance of food across the globe.</p>",
