        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Future Cities, Smart Technologies, and Urban Sociotechnical Systems (JFCSUSS) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary research on urban development, smart technologies, and the complex interplay between social, technical, and environmental systems in cities. The journal provides a platform for rigorous scholarship examining how innovation, data-driven technologies, and sociotechnical infrastructures shape sustainable, resilient, and inclusive urban futures.</p>\n<p>JFCSUSS aims to foster critical understanding of the design, governance, and management of urban environments, emphasizing the integration of technology with social, cultural, and ecological dimensions. The journal encourages contributions that address theoretical, empirical, and applied perspectives on smart cities, urban planning, digital infrastructures, and socio-technical transformations.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JFCSUSS welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case studies, critical reviews, and applied research across a wide spectrum of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Smart Urban Technologies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>IoT, AI, and sensor networks in urban infrastructure</li><li>Data-driven urban management and predictive analytics</li><li>Smart mobility, energy systems, and digital governance</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Urban Sociology and Human-Centered Design:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Social dynamics, equity, and inclusion in urban contexts</li><li>Participatory planning and community engagement</li><li>Urban resilience, adaptation, and quality of life</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Sociotechnical Systems and Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of technological, social, and environmental systems</li><li>Cyber-physical urban infrastructures and digital twins</li><li>Interdisciplinary perspectives from urban studies, engineering, and public policy</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Sustainability, Environment, and Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Sustainable urban development and smart environmental management</li><li>Climate adaptation, green infrastructure, and urban ecology</li><li>Policy frameworks, governance, and regulation of smart cities</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Innovative Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies of urban innovation and technological deployment</li><li>Experimental and practice-led approaches to urban design</li><li>Emerging trends in urban analytics, participatory systems, and smart governance</li></ul>\n<p>JFCSUSS serves as a platform for researchers, policymakers, urban planners, and technologists to share insights on building future-ready, equitable, and technologically advanced urban environments. The journal emphasizes work that bridges theory and practice, fosters interdisciplinary dialogue, and contributes to a deeper understanding of the sociotechnical, cultural, and technological dimensions of modern cities.</p>",
