        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Visual Arts, Cultural Aesthetics, and Societal Imagination (JVACASI) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship at the intersection of visual arts, cultural aesthetics, and societal imagination. The journal provides a platform for critical, theoretical, and practice-based research exploring how artistic expression shapes culture, identity, and social consciousness.</p>\n<p>JVACASI aims to foster understanding of the transformative power of visual arts in reflecting, challenging, and inspiring societal norms, values, and imagination. The journal encourages contributions that integrate perspectives from visual studies, cultural theory, sociology, anthropology, media studies, and related disciplines, emphasizing both historical and contemporary contexts.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JVACASI welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, critical reviews, and practice-led scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Visual Arts and Creative Practices:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Painting, sculpture, photography, digital and multimedia arts</li><li>Experimental, interdisciplinary, and community-based art practices</li><li>Art as a medium for social commentary and cultural critique</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Cultural Aesthetics:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Theoretical frameworks of aesthetic experience and taste</li><li>Cultural symbolism, heritage, and identity in visual practices</li><li>Cross-cultural perspectives on aesthetic appreciation and artistic meaning</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Societal Imagination and Cultural Expression:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Art in shaping collective imagination and social consciousness</li><li>Visual storytelling, narrative arts, and public engagement</li><li>Media, representation, and cultural influence in visual arts</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of visual arts with anthropology, sociology, cultural studies, and media studies</li><li>Digital and participatory methodologies in visual and cultural research</li><li>Practice-led and applied research on art and society</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Community-based and socially engaged art projects</li><li>Innovative use of digital technologies and multimedia in art practice</li><li>Policy, education, and cultural initiatives promoting arts and aesthetics</li></ul>\n<p>JVACASI serves as a platform for scholars, artists, and cultural practitioners to explore the intersections of visual arts, aesthetics, and societal imagination. The journal emphasizes work that bridges theory and practice, fosters interdisciplinary dialogue, and contributes to a deeper understanding of the cultural, social, and transformative roles of visual arts.</p>",
