        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Critical Legal Studies in the Global South (JCLS-GS) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on law, legal theory, and socio-legal practices in the Global South. The journal provides a platform for critical, theory-driven, and empirically grounded research that examines the intersections of law, politics, society, and economy, with particular attention to issues of power, inequality, and social justice.</p>\n<p>JCLS-GS aims to foster critical understanding of the role of law in shaping social structures, governance, and transformative justice in postcolonial, developing, and emerging societies. The journal encourages contributions that integrate doctrinal, theoretical, and interdisciplinary perspectives, bridging law, sociology, political science, anthropology, and development studies.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JCLS-GS welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, critical reviews, and practice-led scholarship across a wide range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Critical Legal Theory:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Postcolonial legal thought and critique</li><li>Law, power, and social hierarchies</li><li>Theoretical frameworks challenging mainstream legal paradigms</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Socio-Legal Studies in the Global South:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Law and development, governance, and social justice</li><li>Access to justice, legal pluralism, and informal legal systems</li><li>Human rights, gender justice, and marginalized communities</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of law with sociology, political science, anthropology, and economics</li><li>Empirical, doctrinal, and comparative methodologies</li><li>Cross-cultural and regional perspectives in legal studies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Law, Policy, and Transformation:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Legal reforms, policy innovation, and governance in the Global South</li><li>Role of law in addressing inequality, poverty, and social exclusion</li><li>Community-based initiatives and participatory legal practices</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on transformative legal practices and litigation</li><li>Impact of globalization, digitalization, and technology on law</li><li>Critical perspectives on contemporary legal challenges in emerging societies</li></ul>\n<p>JCLS-GS serves as a platform for scholars, practitioners, policymakers, and interdisciplinary researchers to critically examine the law’s role in shaping society in the Global South. The journal emphasizes work that bridges theory and practice, fosters critical dialogue, and contributes to a deeper understanding of legal innovation, justice, and social transformation in developing contexts.</p>",
