        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Comparative Journal of Archaeology and Anthropology (CJAA) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship in archaeology, anthropology, and related fields. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining human history, culture, society, and material practices across temporal and spatial contexts, with a focus on comparative and cross-cultural analysis.</p>\n<p>CJAA aims to foster critical understanding of human development, social structures, cultural expression, and material heritage. The journal encourages contributions that integrate theoretical, empirical, and applied perspectives, bridging archaeology, cultural anthropology, social anthropology, ethnography, and heritage studies.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>CJAA welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, critical reviews, and practice-led scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Archaeology:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Prehistoric, historic, and contemporary archaeology</li><li>Material culture, artifacts, and site analysis</li><li>Archaeological methodology, fieldwork, and heritage preservation</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Anthropology:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Cultural, social, and biological anthropology</li><li>Ethnography, human behavior, and societal organization</li><li>Rituals, traditions, and cross-cultural comparative studies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of archaeology and anthropology with sociology, history, and environmental studies</li><li>Digital archaeology, GIS, and technological innovations in research</li><li>Comparative studies of human societies and material cultures</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Heritage, Society, and Public Engagement:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Preservation of cultural and archaeological heritage</li><li>Community-based heritage projects and participatory research</li><li>Policy, ethics, and education in archaeology and anthropology</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on cultural and archaeological discoveries</li><li>Emerging methodologies in fieldwork and digital research</li><li>Interdisciplinary approaches to understanding human evolution, society, and culture</li></ul>\n<p>CJAA serves as a platform for scholars, researchers, and practitioners to explore the intersections of archaeology and anthropology in understanding human history, culture, and society. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters interdisciplinary dialogue, and contributes to a deeper understanding of human development and cultural heritage globally.</p>",
