        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Global Journal of Comparative Folklore, Mythology, and Literary Expression (GJCFMLE) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on folklore, mythology, and literary traditions across cultures. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining the comparative, historical, and cultural dimensions of narrative, myth, and literary expression worldwide.</p>\n<p>GJCFMLE aims to foster critical understanding of how folklore and mythology inform cultural identity, social structures, and artistic creativity. The journal encourages contributions that integrate theoretical, empirical, and interpretive perspectives, bridging literary studies, cultural anthropology, folklore studies, comparative literature, and related disciplines.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>GJCFMLE welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, critical reviews, comparative analyses, and practice-led scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Folklore Studies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Oral traditions, folktales, legends, and narrative practices</li><li>Rituals, customs, and performance traditions</li><li>Regional, indigenous, and marginalized cultural expressions</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Mythology:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Cross-cultural and comparative analysis of myths</li><li>Symbolism, archetypes, and myth in literature and culture</li><li>Mythical narratives in contemporary media and popular culture</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Literary Expression:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Comparative literature, classical and modern texts</li><li>Intersections of folklore, myth, and literary creativity</li><li>Cultural, historical, and social contexts of literary production</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of literary studies, anthropology, cultural studies, and media studies</li><li>Digital humanities, textual analysis, and ethnographic methodologies</li><li>Comparative and cross-cultural methodologies in folklore and literature</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Preservation of intangible cultural heritage and narrative traditions</li><li>Innovative approaches to teaching, documenting, and analyzing folklore and literature</li><li>Impact of globalization, media, and technology on narrative and mythic expression</li></ul>\n<p>GJCFMLE serves as a platform for scholars, literary critics, cultural practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the intersections of folklore, mythology, and literary expression. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, encourages cross-cultural dialogue, and contributes to a deeper understanding of the role of narrative in shaping human culture and creativity.</p>",
