        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Global Journal of Corporate Responsibility, Legal Policy, and Human Development (GJCRLHD) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on corporate governance, legal frameworks, and sustainable human development. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining how corporate responsibility, regulatory policy, and legal innovation intersect to promote ethical business practices, social justice, and inclusive development globally.</p>\n<p>GJCRLHD aims to foster critical understanding of corporate accountability, policy-making, and legal mechanisms that support human development goals. The journal encourages contributions that integrate theoretical, empirical, and policy-oriented perspectives, bridging corporate law, business ethics, public policy, human rights, and development studies.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>GJCRLHD welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, critical reviews, and practice-led scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Corporate Responsibility and Governance:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Ethical, social, and environmental corporate practices</li><li>Corporate social responsibility (CSR) frameworks and compliance</li><li>Stakeholder engagement, transparency, and accountability</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Legal Policy and Regulation:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>National and international corporate law and regulatory frameworks</li><li>Policy development, corporate governance reforms, and enforcement</li><li>Legal mechanisms supporting ethical business and sustainable development</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Human Development and Social Impact:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Linking corporate practices to human rights, health, and education</li><li>Poverty alleviation, inclusive growth, and social equity</li><li>Community engagement and participatory development initiatives</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of law, business ethics, public policy, and development studies</li><li>Empirical, theoretical, and comparative methodologies</li><li>Intersections of technology, corporate practice, and human development</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on corporate accountability and development impact</li><li>Innovative models for CSR, ESG (Environmental, Social, and Governance), and policy implementation</li><li>Evaluating corporate influence on sustainable development goals (SDGs)</li></ul>\n<p>GJCRLHD serves as a platform for scholars, practitioners, policymakers, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the intersections of corporate responsibility, legal policy, and human development. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to a deeper understanding of ethical governance and sustainable societal development.</p>",
