        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Big Data, Society, and Humanities Applications (IJBDSHA) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on the applications of big data in social sciences, humanities, and societal development. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining how large-scale data analytics, computational methodologies, and digital technologies influence human behavior, culture, and social transformation.</p>\n<p>IJBDSHA aims to foster critical understanding of the intersections between big data, society, and the humanities, promoting research that leverages computational insights to address cultural, social, and ethical questions. The journal encourages contributions that integrate theoretical, empirical, and applied approaches, bridging data science, sociology, digital humanities, cultural studies, public policy, and ethics.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>IJBDSHA welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, critical reviews, and practice-led scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Big Data Analytics and Society:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Social network analysis, computational social science, and urban informatics</li><li>Data-driven insights into human behavior, policy, and societal trends</li><li>Ethical, privacy, and governance issues in large-scale data usage</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Humanities Applications:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Digital humanities, computational linguistics, and text/data mining in cultural studies</li><li>Analysis of literature, folklore, history, and cultural artifacts using data-driven methods</li><li>Visualization and interpretation of cultural and social phenomena</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of data science with sociology, anthropology, political science, and cultural studies</li><li>Cross-disciplinary methods combining qualitative and quantitative research</li><li>Comparative, cross-cultural, and global perspectives on data-driven insights</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on big data applications in education, health, governance, and cultural heritage</li><li>Innovative computational tools for social and humanities research</li><li>Impact of artificial intelligence, machine learning, and digital platforms on society</li></ul>\n<p>IJBDSHA serves as a platform for scholars, data scientists, social researchers, and interdisciplinary practitioners to explore the transformative potential of big data in understanding society and culture. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters cross-disciplinary dialogue, and contributes to the responsible, innovative, and socially aware use of data in humanities and societal studies.</p>",
