        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Corporate Governance, Economic Policy, and Legal Ethics (IJCGEPLE) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on corporate governance, economic policy, and legal ethics. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining how corporate practices, regulatory frameworks, and ethical considerations intersect to promote transparency, accountability, and sustainable economic development globally.</p>\n<p>IJCGEPLE aims to foster critical understanding of the theoretical, empirical, and policy dimensions of corporate governance, ethical business conduct, and economic regulation. The journal encourages contributions that integrate law, business studies, economics, public policy, and ethics.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>IJCGEPLE welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, critical reviews, and practice-oriented scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Corporate Governance:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Board structures, corporate accountability, and stakeholder management</li><li>Corporate social responsibility (CSR) and environmental, social, and governance (ESG) initiatives</li><li>Risk management, compliance, and corporate strategy</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Economic Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>National and international economic regulation and policy frameworks</li><li>Financial markets, fiscal policy, and corporate taxation</li><li>Policy impact on business, society, and sustainable development</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Legal Ethics:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Professional responsibility, integrity, and ethical decision-making in corporate law</li><li>Legal frameworks supporting ethical business conduct</li><li>Case studies on corporate malfeasance, compliance, and reform</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of corporate governance, law, economics, and public policy</li><li>Empirical, theoretical, and comparative methodologies</li><li>Global, regional, and cross-cultural perspectives on governance and ethics</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on innovative governance models and regulatory reforms</li><li>Technology, AI, and digital transformation in corporate governance</li><li>Sustainable business practices and their social, economic, and legal implications</li></ul>\n<p>IJCGEPLE serves as a platform for scholars, corporate practitioners, policymakers, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the intersections of governance, policy, and ethics. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to deeper understanding of ethical and sustainable business practices in contemporary economies.</p>",
