        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Cultural Heritage, Museum Studies, and Heritage Management Policy (IJCHMSHMP) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on cultural heritage, museum studies, and heritage management policy. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining the preservation, interpretation, and management of cultural assets, museums, and heritage institutions, with a focus on policy frameworks, sustainable practices, and societal impact.</p>\n<p>IJCHMSHMP aims to foster critical understanding of how cultural heritage is conserved, presented, and governed, emphasizing the interplay between scholarly research, museum practice, and policy development. The journal encourages contributions that integrate theoretical, empirical, and applied approaches, bridging heritage studies, museum studies, anthropology, cultural policy, and public administration.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>IJCHMSHMP welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, critical reviews, and practice-led scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Cultural Heritage Studies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Tangible and intangible heritage preservation</li><li>Cultural identity, memory, and heritage interpretation</li><li>Heritage ethics, cultural diplomacy, and community engagement</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Museum Studies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Curatorial practices, exhibition design, and visitor engagement</li><li>Conservation techniques and collections management</li><li>Innovative approaches in digital and interactive museum experiences</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Heritage Management Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>National and international heritage legislation and regulatory frameworks</li><li>Policy development for sustainable cultural management</li><li>Heritage tourism, funding models, and governance of heritage institutions</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of anthropology, archaeology, architecture, cultural policy, and museum studies</li><li>Comparative, cross-cultural, and international perspectives</li><li>Application of technology, digital tools, and data analytics in heritage management</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on heritage site preservation, museum innovation, and policy implementation</li><li>Strategies for safeguarding cultural heritage in the context of globalization and urbanization</li><li>Innovative models for community participation, education, and outreach in heritage management</li></ul>\n<p>IJCHMSHMP serves as a platform for scholars, heritage professionals, policymakers, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the dynamics of cultural heritage, museum practice, and heritage management policy. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to the sustainable preservation and promotion of cultural assets worldwide.</p>",
