        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Democracy Studies, Constitutional Politics, and Civic Engagement (IJDSCPE) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on democratic governance, constitutional politics, and civic participation. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining the structures, practices, and challenges of democracy, the role of constitutional design in political systems, and mechanisms that foster active citizen engagement.</p>\n<p>IJDSCPE aims to foster critical understanding of the interplay between democratic institutions, constitutional frameworks, and civic practices. The journal encourages contributions that integrate theoretical, empirical, and comparative approaches, bridging political science, law, sociology, public policy, and civic studies.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>IJDSCPE welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, comparative studies, and policy-oriented scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Democracy Studies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Theoretical and practical aspects of democratic governance</li><li>Electoral systems, political representation, and democratic transitions</li><li>Democratization, political participation, and institutional accountability</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Constitutional Politics:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Constitutional design, interpretation, and reform</li><li>Separation of powers, checks and balances, and judicial review</li><li>Rights protection, rule of law, and governance frameworks</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Civic Engagement:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Citizen participation, social movements, and grassroots activism</li><li>Civic education, public deliberation, and community governance</li><li>Digital platforms and technology in promoting civic engagement</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of political science, law, sociology, public policy, and civic studies</li><li>Comparative, empirical, and theoretical methodologies</li><li>Cross-cultural, regional, and global perspectives on democracy and civic life</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on electoral reforms, participatory governance, and civic initiatives</li><li>Innovative approaches to enhancing transparency, accountability, and civic literacy</li><li>Technology-driven solutions for citizen engagement and democratic innovation</li></ul>\n<p>IJDSCPE serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the dynamics of democracy, constitutional politics, and civic participation. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to a deeper understanding of democratic governance, rights protection, and active citizenship.</p>",
