        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Ecological Economics, Natural Resource Studies, and Social Policy (IJEE-NRSP) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on ecological economics, natural resource management, and the formulation of socially inclusive policies. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining the interactions between economic systems, environmental sustainability, natural resource governance, and social policy interventions.</p>\n<p>IJEE-NRSP aims to foster critical understanding of the theoretical, empirical, and policy dimensions of ecological economics and resource management in relation to human well-being and social development. The journal encourages contributions that integrate economics, environmental studies, public policy, social sciences, and development studies.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>IJEE-NRSP welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, critical reviews, and applied scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Ecological Economics:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Sustainable economic models and resource allocation</li><li>Environmental valuation, ecosystem services, and green finance</li><li>Circular economy, ecological accounting, and sustainability metrics</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Natural Resource Studies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Governance and policy for water, energy, forests, and biodiversity</li><li>Community-based resource management and participatory approaches</li><li>Global, regional, and local strategies for sustainable resource utilization</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Social Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Policy interventions linking resource management to human development</li><li>Poverty alleviation, social equity, and inclusive growth strategies</li><li>Social impact assessment and evaluation of development programs</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of economics, environmental science, public policy, and social sciences</li><li>Empirical, theoretical, and comparative methodologies</li><li>Cross-cultural, regional, and global perspectives</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on sustainable resource governance and policy implementation</li><li>Innovative approaches to climate adaptation, conservation, and community development</li><li>Technological and digital solutions in ecological economics and resource management</li></ul>\n<p>IJEE-NRSP serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the dynamic relationships between ecological economics, resource governance, and social policy. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to sustainable, equitable, and socially inclusive development practices.</p>",
