        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Review of Internet Governance, Online Communities, and Social Policy (IRIGOCSP) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on internet governance, digital communities, and the socio-political implications of online interactions. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining how digital platforms, regulatory frameworks, and community dynamics shape social policy, civic engagement, and cultural practices in the digital age.</p>\n<p>IRIGOCSP aims to foster critical understanding of the intersections between technology, governance, and society, promoting research that addresses both normative and empirical questions concerning online platforms and their societal impacts. The journal encourages contributions that integrate perspectives from law, political science, sociology, media studies, information technology, and public policy.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>IRIGOCSP welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, critical reviews, and applied scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Internet Governance:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Policy frameworks, regulation, and digital rights</li><li>Cybersecurity, data protection, and privacy law</li><li>Global, national, and regional approaches to governing the internet</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Online Communities:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Digital social networks, forums, and virtual communities</li><li>Dynamics of participation, collaboration, and collective action</li><li>Identity, culture, and interaction in online spaces</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Social Policy and Digital Society:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Impact of online platforms on social inclusion, equity, and civic engagement</li><li>Policy interventions addressing digital literacy, misinformation, and access</li><li>Technology-driven social innovation and public service delivery</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of law, political science, sociology, information technology, media studies, and public policy</li><li>Comparative, empirical, and theoretical methodologies</li><li>Cross-cultural and global perspectives on digital governance and online communities</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on internet governance, digital platform regulation, and online civic initiatives</li><li>Innovative strategies for fostering safe, inclusive, and equitable digital spaces</li><li>Impact of AI, algorithms, and digital tools on social interactions and governance</li></ul>\n<p>IRIGOCSP serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the dynamic relationships between internet governance, online communities, and social policy. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to the responsible and equitable development of digital societies.</p>",
