        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Review of Legal History, Comparative Governance, and Policy Studies (IRLHCPS) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, committed to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship at the intersection of legal history, governance, and policy analysis. The journal provides a forum for rigorous research examining the historical development of legal systems, comparative governance models, and the implications of these frameworks for contemporary policy-making and institutional reform.</p>\n<p>IRLHCPS seeks to foster critical understanding of how legal traditions, historical precedents, and governance structures shape public policy, social justice, and institutional effectiveness. The journal encourages contributions that combine historical, theoretical, comparative, and empirical approaches, bridging law, political science, public administration, and social sciences.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, comparative analyses, case studies, and policy-oriented scholarship, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Legal History:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Historical evolution of legal doctrines, jurisprudence, and institutions</li><li>Colonial, postcolonial, and transnational legal developments</li><li>Impact of historical legal systems on contemporary governance</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Comparative Governance:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Comparative studies of governmental structures and administrative systems</li><li>Rule of law, accountability, and transparency in different governance contexts</li><li>Institutional reforms and innovations in public administration</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Policy Studies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Policy formulation, implementation, and evaluation</li><li>Legal frameworks and their influence on governance and social outcomes</li><li>Case studies on regulatory, legislative, and administrative reforms</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of law, history, political science, sociology, and public administration</li><li>Empirical, theoretical, and cross-cultural methodologies</li><li>Implications of digital governance, AI, and technological innovation on law and policy</li></ul>\n<p>IRLHCPS serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, legal historians, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the dynamic interactions between law, governance, and policy. The journal emphasizes research that bridges historical insight with contemporary analysis, promotes global dialogue, and contributes to more effective, accountable, and informed governance.</p>",
