        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Intellectual Property, Innovation Policy, and Global Societal Impact (JIPIPSI) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on intellectual property (IP), innovation policy, and the societal impacts of technological and creative advancements. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining how IP frameworks and innovation policies shape global economic development, technological progress, and social equity.</p>\n<p>JIPIPSI aims to foster critical understanding of the intersections between intellectual property law, innovation strategies, and societal outcomes. The journal encourages contributions that integrate legal, economic, policy, and social perspectives, bridging law, economics, business studies, public policy, and technology management.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JIPIPSI welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, policy reviews, and applied scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Intellectual Property:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Copyright, patents, trademarks, trade secrets, and emerging IP frameworks</li><li>IP management in global, national, and regional contexts</li><li>Legal and ethical considerations in IP enforcement and protection</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Innovation Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Policies promoting technological innovation, research and development, and creative industries</li><li>Regulatory frameworks, incentives, and innovation ecosystems</li><li>Strategies for fostering entrepreneurship, startups, and knowledge-based economies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Global Societal Impact:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Socio-economic implications of innovation and IP regimes</li><li>Equity, access, and inclusion in innovation-driven growth</li><li>Technology transfer, sustainable development, and ethical considerations</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of law, economics, public policy, business studies, and technology management</li><li>Comparative, empirical, and theoretical methodologies</li><li>Cross-cultural and global perspectives on IP, innovation, and societal impact</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on IP-driven innovation, technology commercialization, and policy implementation</li><li>Emerging trends such as AI, biotechnology, and digital IP management</li><li>Evaluation of innovation policies’ effectiveness and social consequences</li></ul>\n<p>JIPIPSI serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, legal practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the dynamic interactions between intellectual property, innovation policy, and global societal development. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to sustainable, inclusive, and equitable innovation ecosystems.</p>",
