        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of International Criminal Policy, Peacebuilding, and Governance Ethics (JICPGE) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship at the intersection of international criminal justice, peacebuilding, and ethical governance. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining the design, implementation, and impact of international criminal policies, mechanisms for sustainable peace, and ethical frameworks guiding governance at global, regional, and local levels.</p>\n<p>JICPGE aims to foster critical understanding of the theoretical, legal, and practical dimensions of international criminal justice and peacebuilding, with a focus on ethics, accountability, and human rights. The journal encourages contributions that integrate law, political science, international relations, ethics, and development studies.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JICPGE welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, comparative studies, and policy-oriented scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>International Criminal Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>International criminal law, tribunals, and courts</li><li>Legal frameworks for war crimes, genocide, and crimes against humanity</li><li>Policy-making and enforcement strategies in international justice</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Peacebuilding:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Post-conflict reconstruction, reconciliation, and transitional justice</li><li>Conflict resolution, diplomacy, and humanitarian interventions</li><li>Community-based and regional approaches to sustainable peace</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Governance Ethics:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Ethical frameworks in governance, public administration, and policy-making</li><li>Accountability, transparency, and human rights considerations</li><li>Corruption prevention, institutional integrity, and responsible leadership</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of law, political science, ethics, international relations, and development studies</li><li>Comparative, empirical, and theoretical methodologies</li><li>Cross-national and global perspectives on criminal justice and peacebuilding</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on international tribunals, policy implementation, and peacebuilding initiatives</li><li>Innovations in governance ethics, accountability mechanisms, and legal enforcement</li><li>Role of technology, data, and digital tools in international criminal justice and peace initiatives</li></ul>\n<p>JICPGE serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the complex intersections of criminal justice, peacebuilding, and governance ethics. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to ethical, accountable, and sustainable approaches to international peace and justice.</p>",
