        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Language, Identity, Migration, and Global Intercultural Exchanges (JLIM-GIE) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on the intersections of language, identity, migration, and intercultural communication in a globalized world. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining how language practices, migration experiences, and intercultural exchanges shape individual and collective identities, social integration, and transnational communities.</p>\n<p>JLIM-GIE aims to foster critical understanding of linguistic, cultural, and social processes in migration and intercultural contexts. The journal encourages contributions that integrate perspectives from sociolinguistics, anthropology, migration studies, cultural studies, education, and globalization studies.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JLIM-GIE welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, comparative studies, and applied scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Language and Identity:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Language as a marker of cultural, ethnic, and social identity</li><li>Multilingualism, language shift, and preservation of heritage languages</li><li>Linguistic practices in diaspora and migrant communities</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Migration Studies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Experiences of migrants, refugees, and transnational communities</li><li>Social integration, inclusion, and identity negotiation</li><li>Migration policies, rights, and human mobility</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Global Intercultural Exchanges:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Cross-cultural communication and interaction</li><li>Globalization, cultural hybridity, and transnational networks</li><li>Education, media, and digital communication in intercultural contexts</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of sociolinguistics, anthropology, migration studies, cultural studies, education, and policy studies</li><li>Comparative, ethnographic, and empirical methodologies</li><li>Regional, cross-cultural, and global perspectives</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on language policy, intercultural programs, and diaspora communities</li><li>Technology-mediated communication, digital mobility, and online intercultural exchanges</li><li>Innovations in education, migration management, and cultural integration</li></ul>\n<p>JLIM-GIE serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, educators, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the dynamic relationships between language, identity, migration, and global intercultural exchanges. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to inclusive, culturally sensitive, and linguistically aware approaches to migration and intercultural engagement.</p>",
