        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Peacebuilding, War, and Global Security (JPWGS) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on the dynamics of conflict, peacebuilding strategies, and global security. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining the causes, consequences, and resolution of conflicts, as well as the design and implementation of policies and interventions to promote sustainable peace and international security.</p>\n<p>JPWGS aims to foster critical understanding of the theoretical, political, social, and ethical dimensions of war, peacebuilding, and security studies. The journal encourages contributions that integrate perspectives from international relations, political science, conflict studies, security studies, sociology, law, and development studies.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JPWGS welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, comparative studies, and policy-oriented scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>War and Conflict Studies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Causes and dynamics of intra-state and inter-state conflicts</li><li>Armed conflicts, terrorism, insurgency, and geopolitical tensions</li><li>Humanitarian crises, displacement, and post-conflict challenges</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Peacebuilding:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Conflict resolution, reconciliation, and transitional justice</li><li>Peacekeeping operations, diplomacy, and negotiation strategies</li><li>Community-based, national, and regional peace initiatives</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Global Security:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>International security policy, governance, and strategic studies</li><li>Security ethics, human rights, and the law of armed conflict</li><li>Emerging threats, cyber-security, and technological dimensions of security</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of political science, international relations, sociology, law, and development studies</li><li>Comparative, empirical, and theoretical methodologies</li><li>Cross-cultural and global perspectives on conflict and peace</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on peacebuilding interventions, post-conflict reconstruction, and policy implementation</li><li>Innovations in security governance, risk assessment, and conflict prevention</li><li>Role of technology, media, and data analytics in global security and peacebuilding</li></ul>\n<p>JPWGS serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the complex interactions between conflict, peace, and global security. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters international dialogue, and contributes to the development of effective, ethical, and sustainable strategies for peace and security worldwide.</p>",
