        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Quantum Computation, Society, Ethics, and Global Policy Futures (JQCSE-GPF) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on the scientific, societal, ethical, and policy dimensions of quantum computation. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining the technological development of quantum computing, its ethical implications, societal impacts, and the formulation of forward-looking global policy frameworks.</p>\n<p>JQCSE-GPF aims to foster critical understanding of the interplay between quantum technologies, societal transformations, ethical governance, and global policy futures. The journal encourages contributions that integrate perspectives from quantum physics, computer science, ethics, law, public policy, and social sciences.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JQCSE-GPF welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, policy reviews, and applied scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Quantum Computation and Technology:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Quantum algorithms, architectures, and software development</li><li>Applications in cryptography, AI, optimization, and computational sciences</li><li>Advances in quantum hardware, networking, and hybrid technologies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Societal Impacts:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Influence of quantum computing on industries, economies, and labor markets</li><li>Social equity, digital divides, and accessibility considerations</li><li>Public understanding, education, and societal adaptation to quantum technologies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Ethics and Governance:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Ethical frameworks, responsible innovation, and accountability</li><li>Data privacy, cybersecurity, and dual-use technology concerns</li><li>Policy development for ethical and secure deployment of quantum technologies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Global Policy Futures:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>International governance, regulatory frameworks, and standards for quantum technologies</li><li>Strategic foresight, future-oriented policy design, and scenario planning</li><li>Cross-border collaborations and geopolitical implications of quantum computing</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of physics, computer science, ethics, law, public policy, and social sciences</li><li>Comparative, theoretical, empirical, and scenario-based research methodologies</li><li>Global and cross-cultural perspectives on quantum technologies and societal transformation</li></ul>\n<p>JQCSE-GPF serves as a platform for scholars, technologists, policymakers, ethicists, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the intersections of quantum computation, society, ethics, and global policy. The journal emphasizes research that bridges scientific innovation with societal responsibility, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to the development of forward-looking, ethical, and sustainable strategies for quantum technology deployment.</p>",
