        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Algorithmic Societies, Technological Equity, and Civic Futures (JASTECF) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on the societal, ethical, and civic implications of algorithmic technologies. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining how AI, algorithms, and digital infrastructures shape social structures, equity, governance, and civic participation in contemporary and future societies.</p>\n<p>JASTECF aims to foster critical understanding of the interactions between technology, society, and governance, emphasizing ethical and equitable approaches to algorithmic systems. The journal encourages contributions integrating perspectives from social sciences, technology studies, law, public policy, ethics, and urban studies.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JASTECF welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, case analyses, comparative studies, and applied scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Algorithmic Societies:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Societal impact of AI, algorithms, and digital platforms</li><li>Algorithmic governance, decision-making, and social automation</li><li>Ethics, bias, and transparency in algorithmic systems</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Technological Equity:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Access, inclusivity, and fairness in technology deployment</li><li>Digital divides, socio-economic impacts, and policy interventions</li><li>Social justice, participatory design, and human-centered technology</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Civic Futures:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Governance, civic engagement, and public policy in algorithmic contexts</li><li>Smart cities, digital democracy, and urban technological infrastructures</li><li>Futures studies and scenario planning for equitable digital societies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of social sciences, technology studies, ethics, law, and policy</li><li>Empirical, theoretical, and comparative research methodologies</li><li>Cross-cultural and global perspectives on algorithmic societies and civic futures</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on AI adoption, technological interventions, and policy design</li><li>Evaluation of algorithmic systems in public and private sectors</li><li>Innovative strategies for promoting equity, transparency, and civic empowerment</li></ul>\n<p>JASTECF serves as a platform for scholars, technologists, policymakers, ethicists, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the societal and civic implications of algorithmic technologies. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to the creation of ethical, equitable, and participatory technological futures.</p>",
