        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Coastal Resilience, Marine Ecosystems, and Policy Futures (JCRMEPF) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on coastal and marine sustainability, ecosystem management, and forward-looking policy frameworks. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining the interactions between environmental, social, and economic systems in coastal and marine contexts, with a focus on resilience, conservation, and sustainable development.</p>\n<p>JCRMEPF aims to foster critical understanding of the challenges and opportunities facing coastal regions and marine ecosystems, emphasizing evidence-based, policy-relevant solutions. The journal encourages contributions that integrate perspectives from environmental science, marine biology, ecology, climate studies, policy analysis, and socio-economic development.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JCRMEPF welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, policy analyses, case studies, and applied scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Coastal Resilience:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Climate adaptation, disaster risk reduction, and hazard mitigation</li><li>Coastal zone management, infrastructure resilience, and community preparedness</li><li>Socio-ecological systems and sustainable coastal development</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Marine Ecosystems:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Marine biodiversity, conservation strategies, and ecosystem services</li><li>Fisheries management, habitat restoration, and aquatic resource sustainability</li><li>Impact of human activity and climate change on marine and coastal ecosystems</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Policy Futures:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Environmental governance, regulatory frameworks, and policy innovation</li><li>International agreements, coastal and marine policy integration</li><li>Scenario planning, foresight studies, and adaptive management strategies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of environmental science, ecology, policy studies, economics, and social sciences</li><li>Empirical, theoretical, and comparative research methodologies</li><li>Regional, global, and cross-cultural perspectives on coastal and marine sustainability</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on policy implementation, community resilience, and ecosystem restoration</li><li>Assessment of climate adaptation strategies and sustainable marine practices</li><li>Innovative approaches to governance, technology, and stakeholder engagement in coastal and marine contexts</li></ul>\n<p>JCRMEPF serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, environmental practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore sustainable strategies for coastal and marine resilience. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters international dialogue, and contributes to the development of adaptive, equitable, and science-driven policies for the future of coastal and marine ecosystems.</p>",
