        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Democratic Governance, Policy Futures, and Civic Engagement (JDGPFCE) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on democratic governance, policy innovation, and citizen participation. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining how democratic institutions, governance practices, and civic engagement shape policy-making, societal resilience, and future governance strategies.</p>\n<p>JDGPFCE aims to foster critical understanding of the interactions between governance systems, policy foresight, and active citizenship. The journal encourages contributions integrating perspectives from political science, public policy, law, sociology, civic studies, and governance research.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JDGPFCE welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, policy analyses, case studies, and applied scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Democratic Governance:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Institutional design, accountability, and rule of law</li><li>Governance reforms, transparency, and democratic consolidation</li><li>Comparative studies of democratic systems and governance models</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Policy Futures:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Foresight, scenario planning, and policy innovation</li><li>Governance strategies addressing emerging societal challenges</li><li>Evaluation of policy interventions and sustainable development strategies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Civic Engagement:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Citizen participation, deliberative democracy, and social mobilization</li><li>Civil society initiatives, advocacy, and community governance</li><li>Digital platforms, e-governance, and participatory policymaking</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of political science, public policy, law, sociology, and civic studies</li><li>Empirical, theoretical, and comparative research methodologies</li><li>Global, regional, and cross-cultural perspectives on democratic governance and civic participation</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on policy implementation, civic initiatives, and governance innovations</li><li>Analysis of institutional reforms, public sector strategies, and participatory mechanisms</li><li>Evaluation of future-oriented frameworks promoting inclusive, accountable, and resilient governance</li></ul>\n<p>JDGPFCE serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, civil society leaders, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the dynamics of democratic governance, policy foresight, and citizen engagement. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters international dialogue, and contributes to the development of participatory, accountable, and forward-looking democratic systems.</p>",
