        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Futuristic Social Systems, Cognitive Policy, and Technological Governance (JFSSCTG) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on the design, management, and ethical implications of future-oriented social systems. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining how cognitive science, technological innovation, and governance frameworks shape societal structures, policy-making, and social transformation in the 21st century and beyond.</p>\n<p>JFSSCTG aims to foster critical understanding of the intersections between social systems, cognitive policy, and technological governance. The journal encourages contributions integrating perspectives from sociology, cognitive science, public policy, political science, technology studies, and ethics.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JFSSCTG welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, policy analyses, case studies, and applied scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Futuristic Social Systems:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Design and analysis of adaptive, resilient, and technologically integrated societies</li><li>Social innovation, networked communities, and digital civic ecosystems</li><li>Socio-technical systems, smart cities, and emergent governance models</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Cognitive Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Policy-making informed by cognitive science, behavioral insights, and human decision-making</li><li>AI-assisted governance, data-driven policy frameworks, and anticipatory policy design</li><li>Ethical, societal, and psychological implications of cognitive-informed policies</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Technological Governance:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Governance of emerging technologies, AI, and digital infrastructures</li><li>Regulatory frameworks, standards, and compliance in socio-technical contexts</li><li>Risk management, ethical oversight, and policy foresight in technological innovation</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of sociology, cognitive science, public policy, political science, technology studies, and ethics</li><li>Empirical, theoretical, and comparative research methodologies</li><li>Cross-cultural, regional, and global perspectives on future-oriented social systems and governance</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on smart governance, technological interventions, and policy innovations</li><li>Evaluation of societal impact, ethical frameworks, and regulatory strategies</li><li>Innovative approaches to building adaptive, equitable, and forward-looking social systems</li></ul>\n<p>JFSSCTG serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, technologists, ethicists, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the transformative intersections of society, cognition, and technology. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to the development of resilient, ethical, and future-ready social systems.</p>",
