        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Marine Science, Coastal Policy, and Socio-Ecological Futures (JMSCPSEF) is a peer-reviewed, regularly published academic journal under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship on marine science, coastal management, and the socio-ecological dynamics shaping coastal and marine futures. The journal provides a platform for rigorous research examining how ecological, policy, and societal factors interact to influence the sustainability, resilience, and governance of marine and coastal environments globally.</p>\n<p>JMSCPSEF aims to foster critical understanding of the interactions between marine ecosystems, coastal governance, and socio-ecological transformation. The journal encourages contributions integrating perspectives from marine biology, environmental science, oceanography, policy studies, sociology, and sustainability science.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JMSCPSEF welcomes original research articles, conceptual studies, policy analyses, case studies, and applied scholarship across a broad range of topics, including but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Marine Science:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Marine ecosystems, biodiversity, and ecological health</li><li>Oceanographic studies, marine resource management, and conservation science</li><li>Climate change impacts, resilience, and adaptation in marine environments</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Coastal Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Coastal governance, planning, and regulatory frameworks</li><li>Sustainable development policies for coastal and marine regions</li><li>Legal, institutional, and community-based approaches to coastal management</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Socio-Ecological Futures:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Human-environment interactions and community resilience</li><li>Socio-economic impacts of environmental change and coastal development</li><li>Strategies for sustainable, adaptive, and equitable socio-ecological futures</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Interdisciplinary Approaches:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Integration of marine science, environmental policy, sociology, and sustainability studies</li><li>Empirical, theoretical, and comparative research methodologies</li><li>Regional, global, and cross-cultural perspectives on coastal and marine governance</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Applied and Emerging Research:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Case studies on marine conservation, coastal adaptation, and policy interventions</li><li>Evaluation of socio-ecological outcomes, sustainability programs, and governance models</li><li>Innovative approaches to harmonizing ecological integrity, societal needs, and governance</li></ul>\n<p>JMSCPSEF serves as a platform for scholars, policymakers, environmental practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore the transformative intersections of marine science, coastal policy, and socio-ecological futures. The journal emphasizes research that bridges theory and practice, fosters global dialogue, and contributes to the development of resilient, sustainable, and ethically informed marine and coastal governance strategies.</p>",
