        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Disability Rights and Legal Studies (JDRLS) is a peer-reviewed academic journal published under Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing critical scholarship on disability rights, law, and inclusive governance. The journal provides a global platform for legal scholars, policymakers, activists, and interdisciplinary researchers to engage with the evolving legal, social, and ethical dimensions of disability.</p>\n<p>JDRLS seeks to explore the intersections of disability rights with constitutional law, human rights, international law, and comparative legal studies, while also addressing the challenges of policy implementation, access to justice, and equality in diverse socio-political contexts.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>JDRLS invites original research articles, case studies, doctrinal analyses, policy reviews, and interdisciplinary contributions in areas including (but not limited to):</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Disability Rights in Legal Frameworks</li><li>Constitutional guarantees and legal protections for persons with disabilities</li><li>National, regional, and international disability rights instruments (e.g., CRPD)</li><li>Comparative disability law and governance models</li><li>Access to Justice and Legal Empowerment</li><li>Barriers to legal remedies and participation in justice systems</li><li>Legal aid, advocacy, and community-based approaches to disability rights</li><li>Judicial interpretations and landmark cases on disability rights</li><li>Policy, Governance, and Implementation</li><li>Disability-inclusive public policy and social welfare systems</li><li>Inclusive education, healthcare, employment, and accessibility rights</li><li>Monitoring and enforcement of disability rights obligations</li><li>Interdisciplinary and Critical Perspectives</li><li>Intersectionality of disability with gender, class, race, and migration</li><li>Disability studies, sociology of law, and human development approaches</li><li>Ethical and philosophical debates on autonomy, dignity, and inclusion</li><li>Global and Regional Issues</li><li>Disability rights in the Global South and marginalized communities</li><li>Transnational advocacy networks and grassroots disability movements</li><li>Emerging challenges in digital accessibility, technology, and AI governance</li><li>JDRLS positions itself as a leading forum for both theoretical exploration and practical policy debate, fostering inclusive knowledge production that contributes to equality, dignity, and justice for persons with disabilities worldwide.</li></ul>",
