        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Public Interest Litigation and Governance (JPILG) is a peer-reviewed academic journal published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, focused on the study of public interest litigation (PIL) as a mechanism for promoting justice, accountability, and good governance. The journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, practitioners, and interdisciplinary researchers to explore how courts, legal frameworks, and governance structures interact to address public concerns, protect rights, and advance democratic principles.</p>\n<p>JPILG encourages critical analyses of the doctrinal, social, and policy dimensions of PIL, including its role in safeguarding human rights, promoting social justice, and influencing governance practices. Contributions integrating law, political science, public administration, sociology, and human rights studies are particularly welcome.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, comparative analyses, theoretical essays, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Public Interest Litigation</li><li>Doctrinal and procedural analysis of PIL</li><li>Landmark cases and judicial activism</li><li>PIL as a tool for promoting environmental protection, social justice, and public welfare</li><li>Governance and Accountability</li><li>Judicial oversight of executive and legislative actions</li><li>Transparency, anti-corruption, and administrative reforms</li><li>Legal frameworks supporting democratic governance</li><li>Human Rights and Social Justice</li><li>Protection of civil, political, economic, and environmental rights</li><li>Access to justice for marginalized and vulnerable populations</li><li>Evaluation of PIL’s impact on policy and societal outcomes</li><li>Interdisciplinary and Comparative Perspectives</li><li>Socio-legal, political, and ethical analyses of litigation</li><li>Comparative studies of PIL and governance practices across jurisdictions</li><li>Integration of law, social policy, and public administration insights</li><li>Emerging Challenges</li><li>PIL in digital governance, climate justice, and emerging socio-legal contexts</li><li>Innovations in legal advocacy, community participation, and policy implementation</li><li>Assessing effectiveness and societal impact of strategic litigation</li><li>JPILG aims to bridge theory and practice, foster interdisciplinary dialogue, and contribute to the development of robust legal and governance frameworks that uphold justice, accountability, and public welfare.</li></ul>",
