        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Behavioral and Experimental Economics (JBEE) is a peer-reviewed academic journal published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing research on human decision-making, behavioral insights, and experimental methods in economics. The journal provides a platform for scholars, policymakers, and practitioners to examine how cognitive, psychological, and social factors influence economic behavior, market dynamics, and policy outcomes.</p>\n<p>JBEE aims to bridge theoretical and empirical research, promoting interdisciplinary scholarship that integrates behavioral economics, experimental studies, psychology, sociology, and public policy. Contributions that enhance the understanding of human behavior in economic contexts, improve policy design, or inform market interventions are particularly welcome.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal welcomes original research articles, experimental studies, field and lab experiments, theoretical essays, and policy analyses in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Behavioral Economics</li><li>Cognitive biases, heuristics, and decision-making processes</li><li>Behavioral interventions, nudges, and incentive structures</li><li>Risk perception, time preferences, and social preferences</li><li>Experimental Economics</li><li>Laboratory, field, and online experiments in economic contexts</li><li>Testing economic theories through controlled experimental designs</li><li>Behavioral game theory, auctions, and market experiments</li><li>Behavioral Policy and Applied Research</li><li>Behavioral insights for public policy, finance, and organizational decision-making</li><li>Experimental evaluation of programs and policy interventions</li><li>Implications of behavioral research for social welfare and economic development</li><li>Interdisciplinary Perspectives</li><li>Integration of psychology, sociology, neuroscience, and economics</li><li>Behavioral finance, consumer behavior, and labor economics</li><li>Cross-cultural and comparative studies on human economic behavior</li><li>Emerging Issues and Innovations</li><li>Digital platforms, AI, and behavioral implications in online economies</li><li>Sustainability, environmental behavior, and behavioral interventions for global challenges</li><li>Novel experimental methodologies and technological tools in economics research</li><li>JBEE serves as a leading forum for rigorous, evidence-based research that deepens the understanding of human behavior in economic systems, informs policymaking, and advances both theoretical and applied economics.</li></ul>",
