          "title": "Comparative AI Regulation: EU, US, China, and India",
          "image": "images/arts.png",
          "fullContent": "<p>This comparative study maps AI regulations across four major jurisdictions. The EU takes a risk-based approach, the US is sectoral, China emphasizes state security, and India focuses on innovation. We identify best practices for developing countries.</p>"
