        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Global Journal of Climate Change Policy, Environmental Management, and Sustainable Communities (GJCCP-EMSC) is a peer-reviewed academic journal published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary research on climate change policy, environmental governance, and the development of sustainable, resilient communities. The journal provides a platform for scholars, policymakers, environmental scientists, urban planners, and social researchers to examine the interactions between climate strategies, environmental management practices, and societal transformation toward sustainability.</p>\n<p>GJCCP-EMSC seeks to foster research that integrates policy analysis, ecological science, socio-economic studies, and community-focused approaches to address climate challenges. Contributions that explore sustainable urban and rural development, climate resilience, and innovative environmental management strategies are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, policy evaluations, theoretical essays, and interdisciplinary reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Climate Change Policy</li><li>National and international climate governance frameworks</li><li>Policy design, implementation, and assessment for mitigation and adaptation</li><li>Legal, institutional, and regulatory mechanisms for climate action</li><li>Environmental Management</li><li>Sustainable resource management, conservation, and ecological restoration</li><li>Environmental impact assessment, monitoring, and governance</li><li>Integration of environmental management with technological and social innovations</li><li>Sustainable Communities</li><li>Development of resilient urban and rural communities</li><li>Community-based adaptation, participatory planning, and capacity building</li><li>Socio-economic and cultural dimensions of sustainability</li><li>Interdisciplinary and Comparative Research</li><li>Integration of environmental science, sociology, economics, law, and public policy</li><li>Comparative analyses of climate strategies, governance models, and sustainable practices</li><li>Emerging trends in climate resilience, green technology, and community empowerment</li><li>GJCCP-EMSC serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines climate change policy, environmental management, and sustainable community development, promoting evidence-based, equitable, and forward-looking solutions for global environmental challenges.</li></ul>",
