        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Technology, Data Protection and Law (IJTDPL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship at the intersection of technology, law, and data governance. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, technologists, policymakers, and practitioners to critically examine regulatory frameworks, emerging technologies, and legal challenges related to data protection, cybersecurity, and digital innovation.</p>\n<p>IJTDPL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that bridges law, information technology, and policy analysis, promoting evidence-based insights into the ethical, legal, and societal implications of technological development. Contributions that analyze emerging technologies, data privacy regimes, cybersecurity regulations, and digital rights are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, comparative legal analyses, policy reviews, and critical essays in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Data Protection and Privacy Law</h4>\n<p>International and national frameworks for data protection</p>\n<p>Compliance, enforcement, and regulatory challenges</p>\n<p>Privacy by design, consent mechanisms, and data ethics</p>\n<h4>2. Cybersecurity and Digital Governance</h4>\n<p>Legal aspects of cybercrime, network security, and critical infrastructure protection</p>\n<p>Regulation of digital platforms and emerging technologies</p>\n<p>Standards, best practices, and legal liability in cybersecurity</p>\n<h4>3. Technology and Society</h4>\n<p>Ethical and socio-legal implications of AI, IoT, and big data</p>\n<p>Algorithmic accountability, transparency, and fairness</p>\n<p>Digital rights, freedom of expression, and access to information</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Cross-border data flows and international legal harmonization</p>\n<p>Comparative studies of national data protection laws and technological regulations</p>\n<p>Global governance, policy innovation, and international cooperation</p>\n<h4>5. Legal and Policy Innovation</h4>\n<p>Emerging legal frameworks for digital transformation</p>\n<p>Policy strategies for secure, equitable, and responsible technology use</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary approaches combining law, technology, and social sciences</p>\n<p>IJTDPL serves as a leading forum for research that critically examines the intersection of technology and law, fostering informed debate, promoting policy innovation, and contributing to the development of a secure, accountable, and rights-respecting digital ecosystem.</p>",
