        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Blockchain, FinTech and Law Review (IJBFLR) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship at the intersection of law, financial technology, and blockchain innovations. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, financial technologists, policymakers, and industry practitioners to critically analyze regulatory, legal, and technological challenges arising from blockchain, cryptocurrencies, digital finance, and emerging FinTech solutions.</p>\n<p>IJBFLR encourages research that bridges theory and practice, exploring how technological innovations transform financial systems, legal frameworks, and governance models. Submissions examining blockchain-based applications, decentralized finance, smart contracts, regulatory compliance, and the ethical, social, and legal implications of FinTech adoption are particularly welcome.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, comparative legal analyses, policy reviews, and critical essays in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Blockchain Technology and Legal Frameworks</h4>\n<p>Legal and regulatory implications of blockchain adoption</p>\n<p>Smart contracts, tokenization, and decentralized applications</p>\n<p>Governance, compliance, and dispute resolution in blockchain ecosystems</p>\n<h4>2. FinTech Innovation and Financial Law</h4>\n<p>Cryptocurrencies, digital payment systems, and online banking regulations</p>\n<p>Peer-to-peer lending, crowdfunding, and decentralized finance (DeFi)</p>\n<p>Risk management, anti-money laundering (AML), and fraud prevention</p>\n<h4>3. Data, Privacy, and Security in FinTech</h4>\n<p>Cybersecurity and data protection in digital financial platforms</p>\n<p>Privacy compliance, GDPR, and emerging regulatory standards</p>\n<p>Technological risks, resilience, and legal accountability</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Cross-border regulation of blockchain and FinTech activities</p>\n<p>Comparative analysis of national and international FinTech laws</p>\n<p>Global financial governance and regulatory harmonization</p>\n<h4>5. Ethics, Policy, and Socio-Legal Implications</h4>\n<p>Ethical considerations in algorithmic finance and blockchain applications</p>\n<p>Financial inclusion, digital literacy, and socio-economic impacts</p>\n<p>Policy innovation and interdisciplinary approaches combining law, finance, and technology</p>\n<p>IJBFLR serves as a leading forum for research that critically examines the intersection of blockchain, FinTech, and law, contributing to innovative, secure, and equitable financial and legal practices worldwide.</p>",
