        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Privacy, Surveillance and Law (IJPSL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to exploring the legal, ethical, and societal dimensions of privacy and surveillance in contemporary society. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for scholars, legal practitioners, technologists, and policymakers to critically examine regulatory frameworks, technological developments, and policy challenges relating to personal data, digital surveillance, and individual rights.</p>\n<p>IJPSL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that bridges law, technology, and social sciences, promoting evidence-based insights into the implications of surveillance technologies, data collection practices, and privacy protection measures. Contributions analyzing emerging trends in digital privacy, accountability frameworks, surveillance governance, and human rights implications are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, comparative legal analyses, policy reviews, and critical essays in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Privacy Law and Data Protection</h4>\n<p>National and international frameworks for data privacy and protection</p>\n<p>Compliance, enforcement, and regulatory challenges</p>\n<p>Emerging issues in digital rights, consent, and privacy by design</p>\n<h4>2. Surveillance, Monitoring, and Governance</h4>\n<p>Legal and ethical aspects of state and corporate surveillance</p>\n<p>Mass surveillance, algorithmic monitoring, and predictive analytics</p>\n<p>Accountability, transparency, and oversight mechanisms</p>\n<h4>3. Technology, Security, and Digital Rights</h4>\n<p>Cybersecurity, encryption, and secure data management</p>\n<p>Human rights implications of surveillance technologies</p>\n<p>Freedom of expression, access to information, and digital liberties</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Cross-border data flows, global privacy standards, and international regulation</p>\n<p>Comparative studies of national privacy and surveillance laws</p>\n<p>Policy harmonization, international cooperation, and digital governance</p>\n<h4>5. Ethical, Social, and Policy Implications</h4>\n<p>Societal impact of pervasive monitoring and privacy intrusions</p>\n<p>Policy innovation to balance security, privacy, and rights</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary approaches combining law, technology, and ethics</p>\n<p>IJPSL serves as a leading forum for critical scholarship on privacy, surveillance, and law, promoting informed debate, policy innovation, and the protection of fundamental rights in the digital age.</p>",
