        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Space Law and Emerging Technologies (IJSL-ET) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship at the intersection of space law, emerging technologies, and regulatory frameworks. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, technologists, and industry practitioners to critically examine legal, ethical, and policy issues arising from outer space activities and emerging technological innovations.</p>\n<p>IJSL-ET seeks to foster research that bridges law, science, and technology, promoting evidence-based insights into the governance, regulation, and ethical implications of space exploration, satellite systems, and advanced technological developments. Contributions exploring legal challenges, policy frameworks, and technological innovations in outer space and related domains are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, comparative legal analyses, policy reviews, and critical essays in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Space Law and Governance</h4>\n<p>National and international legal frameworks governing outer space activities</p>\n<p>Space treaties, conventions, and regulatory compliance</p>\n<p>Liability, dispute resolution, and governance mechanisms</p>\n<h4>2. Emerging Space Technologies</h4>\n<p>Satellite communications, navigation, and remote sensing</p>\n<p>Space exploration technologies, robotics, and AI applications in space</p>\n<p>Technological innovations and their legal, ethical, and regulatory implications</p>\n<h4>3. Security, Ethics, and Policy</h4>\n<p>Space security, militarization, and dual-use technology regulation</p>\n<p>Ethical considerations in space exploration and technological deployment</p>\n<p>Policy frameworks for sustainable and responsible space activities</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Cross-border space governance and international cooperation</p>\n<p>Comparative studies of national and regional space laws</p>\n<p>Global policy harmonization and space diplomacy</p>\n<h4>5. Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Intersection of space law with technology, economics, and environmental policy</p>\n<p>Legal and regulatory challenges of commercial space activities</p>\n<p>Socio-legal analysis of emerging trends in outer space governance</p>\n<p>IJSL-ET serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of law, technology, and outer space, fostering innovation, accountability, and sustainable governance in emerging space activities.</p>",
