        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Review of Humanitarian Law (IRHL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to the study and advancement of international humanitarian law (IHL) and related legal frameworks governing armed conflicts, human rights, and humanitarian protection. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for scholars, legal practitioners, policymakers, and humanitarian actors to critically examine the legal, ethical, and practical dimensions of humanitarian law.</p>\n<p>IRHL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates legal analysis, policy considerations, and field experiences, promoting evidence-based insights into the protection of individuals and communities affected by armed conflict. Contributions addressing the evolving challenges of warfare, accountability mechanisms, compliance with IHL, and the intersection of humanitarian law with human rights and international criminal law are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, comparative legal analyses, policy reviews, and critical essays in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. International Humanitarian Law (IHL)</h4>\n<p>Legal frameworks governing armed conflict, occupation, and hostilities</p>\n<p>Protections for civilians, combatants, and vulnerable populations</p>\n<p>Compliance, enforcement, and accountability mechanisms</p>\n<h4>2. Human Rights and Humanitarian Protection</h4>\n<p>Intersection of IHL with international human rights law</p>\n<p>Protection of refugees, displaced persons, and civilians in conflict zones</p>\n<p>Legal obligations of states, international organizations, and non-state actors</p>\n<h4>3. International Criminal Law and Accountability</h4>\n<p>War crimes, crimes against humanity, and genocide</p>\n<p>Role of international courts, tribunals, and hybrid justice mechanisms</p>\n<p>Investigations, prosecutions, and enforcement of humanitarian law violations</p>\n<h4>4. Emerging Challenges and Contemporary Issues</h4>\n<p>Cyber warfare, autonomous weapons, and technological implications for IHL</p>\n<p>Asymmetric warfare, terrorism, and non-traditional conflict scenarios</p>\n<p>Policy and legal reforms to address evolving humanitarian challenges</p>\n<h4>5. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative analysis of national implementation of IHL</p>\n<p>Cross-border humanitarian law issues and international cooperation</p>\n<p>Global standards, treaties, and conventions in humanitarian law</p>\n<p>IRHL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the theory and practice of humanitarian law, contributing to the development of effective, accountable, and rights-based responses to contemporary humanitarian challenges.</p>",
