        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Anti-Corruption Law and Policy (IJACLP) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the legal, regulatory, and policy frameworks addressing corruption in public and private sectors. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, practitioners, and social scientists to critically examine the causes, consequences, and control mechanisms of corruption, promoting transparency, accountability, and good governance.</p>\n<p>IJACLP encourages research that bridges theory, practice, and policy, exploring innovative strategies, comparative legal analyses, and evidence-based interventions to combat corruption globally. Contributions addressing anti-corruption legislation, regulatory compliance, enforcement mechanisms, ethical governance, and socio-legal implications are particularly welcome.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Anti-Corruption Law and Regulation</h4>\n<p>National and international anti-corruption frameworks</p>\n<p>Legislative measures, compliance, and enforcement mechanisms</p>\n<p>Judicial and regulatory approaches to corruption control</p>\n<h4>2. Governance, Ethics, and Accountability</h4>\n<p>Corporate governance, transparency, and ethical standards</p>\n<p>Public sector integrity, accountability, and policy reforms</p>\n<p>Anti-corruption strategies and best practices</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Cross-country analyses of anti-corruption laws and policies</p>\n<p>International conventions, treaties, and transnational cooperation</p>\n<p>Global standards for integrity, compliance, and enforcement</p>\n<h4>4. Policy Innovation and Socio-Legal Implications</h4>\n<p>Policy interventions for corruption prevention and risk management</p>\n<p>Socio-economic impacts of corruption and anti-corruption measures</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary approaches linking law, policy, and social sciences</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges in Anti-Corruption</h4>\n<p>Digital governance, blockchain, and technology-enabled accountability</p>\n<p>Whistleblowing, investigative mechanisms, and civil society roles</p>\n<p>Corruption in new sectors, complex financial systems, and international trade</p>\n<p>IJACLP serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the law and policy of anti-corruption, fostering research, dialogue, and practical solutions aimed at promoting integrity, transparency, and accountable governance worldwide.</p>",
