        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Law and Minority Rights (IJLMR) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the legal, social, and policy issues affecting minority communities worldwide. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, human rights practitioners, and social scientists to critically examine the protection, promotion, and enforcement of minority rights under domestic and international law.</p>\n<p>IJLMR seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, social policy, and human rights perspectives, promoting evidence-based insights into the challenges faced by minority communities and the mechanisms for safeguarding their rights. Contributions analyzing legal protections, social justice, anti-discrimination policies, and comparative minority rights frameworks are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, comparative legal analyses, theoretical essays, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Legal Frameworks and Minority Rights</h4>\n<p>National and international legal protections for minority groups</p>\n<p>Constitutional guarantees, human rights instruments, and treaties</p>\n<p>Legal remedies, enforcement mechanisms, and access to justice</p>\n<h4>2. Anti-Discrimination and Social Inclusion</h4>\n<p>Protection against racial, ethnic, religious, linguistic, or gender-based discrimination</p>\n<p>Policies and programs promoting inclusion, equity, and social justice</p>\n<p>Legal and policy strategies to address systemic inequalities</p>\n<h4>3. Cultural, Religious, and Linguistic Rights</h4>\n<p>Preservation of minority languages, cultures, and traditions</p>\n<p>Religious freedoms and intercultural dialogue</p>\n<p>Rights to education, cultural participation, and representation</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of minority rights across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International human rights law and minority protection</p>\n<p>Global best practices, policy harmonization, and advocacy strategies</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Policy Innovations</h4>\n<p>Migration, displacement, and refugee rights of minorities</p>\n<p>Intersection of minority rights with technology, digital inclusion, and socio-economic development</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary approaches combining law, social sciences, and policy research</p>\n<p>IJLMR serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines law, policy, and social frameworks affecting minority communities, fostering research, debate, and actionable strategies to advance equality, justice, and human rights worldwide.</p>",
