        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Global Journal of Corporate Social Responsibility and Law (GJCSRL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the intersection of corporate governance, social responsibility, and legal frameworks. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, business ethicists, policymakers, corporate practitioners, and social scientists to critically examine legal obligations, ethical standards, and regulatory mechanisms governing corporate social responsibility (CSR).</p>\n<p>GJCSRL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, business ethics, sustainability, and social policy, promoting evidence-based insights into responsible corporate behavior and legal compliance. Contributions analyzing CSR regulation, corporate governance, ethical practices, stakeholder engagement, and socio-legal implications of corporate activities are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Corporate Governance and CSR Law</h4>\n<p>Legal frameworks governing corporate social responsibility</p>\n<p>Compliance, enforcement, and accountability mechanisms</p>\n<p>Corporate governance, transparency, and stakeholder rights</p>\n<h4>2. Business Ethics and Social Responsibility</h4>\n<p>Ethical decision-making in corporate practice</p>\n<p>Social and environmental responsibility initiatives</p>\n<p>Corporate accountability to communities and society at large</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of CSR laws and regulations across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International standards, guidelines, and conventions on corporate responsibility</p>\n<p>Cross-border CSR compliance and global governance strategies</p>\n<h4>4. Policy, Regulation, and Sustainable Development</h4>\n<p>CSR policies aligned with sustainable development goals (SDGs)</p>\n<p>Regulatory innovations and best practices for responsible corporate behavior</p>\n<p>Role of law in promoting environmental, social, and economic sustainability</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Technology, digital transformation, and CSR compliance</p>\n<p>Social impact measurement, reporting, and accountability</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, policy, business ethics, and social sciences</p>\n<p>GJCSRL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the legal, ethical, and policy dimensions of corporate social responsibility, fostering research, debate, and practical solutions to enhance corporate accountability and sustainable development globally.</p>",
