        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Health, Medicine and Bioethics Law (IJHMBL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary scholarship at the intersection of health law, medical ethics, and bioethics. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, medical professionals, bioethicists, policymakers, and researchers to critically examine the legal, ethical, and societal implications of healthcare practices, biomedical research, and public health policies.</p>\n<p>IJHMBL seeks to foster research that integrates law, medical ethics, and public health policy, promoting evidence-based insights into ethical dilemmas, legal frameworks, and governance mechanisms in health and medicine. Contributions analyzing bioethical principles, healthcare regulation, patient rights, clinical practice, and emerging biomedical technologies are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Health Law and Policy</h4>\n<p>National and international legal frameworks governing healthcare</p>\n<p>Regulation of medical practice, hospitals, and health institutions</p>\n<p>Public health law, emergency response, and pandemic management</p>\n<h4>2. Medical Ethics and Bioethics</h4>\n<p>Ethical considerations in clinical practice and medical research</p>\n<p>Patient autonomy, informed consent, and confidentiality</p>\n<p>Allocation of scarce resources and end-of-life decisions</p>\n<h4>3. Biomedical Technologies and Legal Governance</h4>\n<p>Regulation of biotechnology, genomics, and medical devices</p>\n<p>Ethical and legal implications of AI, digital health, and telemedicine</p>\n<p>Research ethics, clinical trials, and human subject protection</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of health, medicine, and bioethics laws</p>\n<p>International treaties, conventions, and global health governance</p>\n<p>Cross-border public health policies and harmonization</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Public health ethics, health equity, and social justice in medicine</p>\n<p>Policy and legal responses to emerging infectious diseases</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research integrating law, medicine, ethics, and public health</p>\n<p>IJHMBL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of health, medicine, and bioethics law, fostering research, debate, and practical solutions to promote ethical, equitable, and legally sound healthcare globally.</p>",
