        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Disaster Management, Law and Policy (IJDMLP) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the legal, policy, and governance dimensions of disaster management. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, disaster management practitioners, and researchers to critically examine the regulatory frameworks, risk reduction strategies, and policy interventions addressing natural and human-made disasters.</p>\n<p>IJDMLP seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, public policy, risk management, and socio-economic perspectives, promoting evidence-based insights into effective disaster preparedness, response, recovery, and mitigation. Contributions analyzing legal frameworks, governance mechanisms, disaster risk reduction strategies, and policy innovations are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Disaster Law and Governance</h4>\n<p>National and international legal frameworks for disaster management</p>\n<p>Regulatory compliance, liability, and enforcement mechanisms</p>\n<p>Institutional governance and coordination in disaster risk management</p>\n<h4>2. Disaster Policy and Risk Reduction</h4>\n<p>Policy strategies for prevention, preparedness, response, and recovery</p>\n<p>Risk assessment, early warning systems, and emergency planning</p>\n<p>Community resilience, capacity building, and social protection</p>\n<h4>3. Human Rights and Social Justice in Disasters</h4>\n<p>Protection of vulnerable populations during disasters</p>\n<p>Ethical and equitable approaches to disaster response and relief</p>\n<p>Intersection of disaster management with human rights and social justice</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of disaster laws and policies across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International agreements, conventions, and cooperation in disaster management</p>\n<p>Global standards and best practices for disaster risk governance</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Climate change, environmental hazards, and disaster risk</p>\n<p>Technological innovations in disaster management and emergency response</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research combining law, policy, social sciences, and environmental studies</p>\n<p>IJDMLP serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of law, policy, and disaster management, fostering research, debate, and practical solutions to enhance resilience, accountability, and effective disaster governance worldwide.</p>",
