        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Constitutional, Comparative &amp; Regional Law (IJCCRL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship in constitutional law, comparative legal studies, and regional legal systems. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, practitioners, policymakers, and researchers to critically examine constitutional principles, comparative legal frameworks, and region-specific legal issues.</p>\n<p>IJCCRL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates legal theory, jurisprudence, and socio-political analysis, promoting evidence-based insights into constitutional interpretation, legal reforms, and the development of regional legal systems. Contributions analyzing constitutional governance, comparative law, judicial decisions, and regional legal integration are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Constitutional Law</h4>\n<p>Fundamental rights, constitutional interpretation, and judicial review</p>\n<p>Separation of powers, federalism, and governance structures</p>\n<p>Constitutional reforms, amendments, and emerging challenges</p>\n<h4>2. Comparative Law</h4>\n<p>Cross-jurisdictional analysis of legal principles and systems</p>\n<p>Comparative studies of constitutional and statutory law</p>\n<p>Lessons from international and regional legal practices</p>\n<h4>3. Regional Legal Studies</h4>\n<p>Law and governance in specific regions, states, or unions</p>\n<p>Regional integration, treaties, and intergovernmental legal frameworks</p>\n<p>Socio-legal, cultural, and historical influences on regional law</p>\n<h4>4. Human Rights, Democracy, and Rule of Law</h4>\n<p>Protection of civil, political, and socio-economic rights</p>\n<p>Rule of law, accountability, and democratic governance</p>\n<p>Judicial activism, constitutional litigation, and legal innovations</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Issues and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Constitutional and legal responses to technological, social, and political changes</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, politics, and social sciences</p>\n<p>Policy recommendations, law reform, and practical governance solutions</p>\n<p>IJCCRL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines constitutional, comparative, and regional legal systems, fostering research, debate, and practical insights into legal development, governance, and reform worldwide.</p>",
