        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Federalism, Devolution and Law (IJFDL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on federalism, devolution, and related legal frameworks. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, governance experts, and researchers to critically examine the legal, constitutional, and policy dimensions of federal and devolved systems of governance.</p>\n<p>IJFDL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, political science, and public policy, promoting evidence-based insights into the design, implementation, and challenges of federal and devolved governance structures. Contributions analyzing constitutional provisions, intergovernmental relations, decentralization, and comparative studies of federal and devolved systems are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Federalism and Constitutional Law</h4>\n<p>Principles, structures, and functions of federal and unitary systems</p>\n<p>Constitutional design, division of powers, and intergovernmental relations</p>\n<p>Judicial interpretation and legal reforms in federal contexts</p>\n<h4>2. Devolution and Local Governance</h4>\n<p>Legal and policy frameworks for devolution of powers</p>\n<p>Local governance, autonomy, and accountability mechanisms</p>\n<p>Decentralization and public administration reforms</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of federal and devolved systems across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International experiences, treaties, and cooperative governance models</p>\n<p>Policy lessons and best practices in federalism and devolution</p>\n<h4>4. Human Rights, Democracy, and Rule of Law</h4>\n<p>Protection of minority rights and equitable resource distribution</p>\n<p>Democratic governance, transparency, and accountability</p>\n<p>Legal safeguards in multi-tier governance systems</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Federal and devolved governance in response to social, economic, and technological change</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, public policy, political science, and administration</p>\n<p>Policy recommendations and practical solutions for effective governance</p>\n<p>IJFDL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines federalism, devolution, and law, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to enhance governance, legal certainty, and democratic accountability worldwide.</p>",
