        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Parliamentary Studies and Law (IJPSL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on parliamentary governance, legislative processes, and legal frameworks. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, political scientists, legislators, policymakers, and researchers to critically examine the law-making process, parliamentary oversight, and the constitutional and legal dimensions of legislative governance.</p>\n<p>IJPSL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, political science, and public policy, promoting evidence-based insights into the functioning, accountability, and effectiveness of parliaments. Contributions analyzing legislative processes, parliamentary law, comparative parliamentary studies, and institutional reforms are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Parliamentary Law and Governance</h4>\n<p>Legal frameworks governing parliaments and legislative bodies</p>\n<p>Parliamentary procedures, rules of law, and legislative drafting</p>\n<p>Oversight, accountability, and checks and balances</p>\n<h4>2. Legislative Processes and Institutional Functioning</h4>\n<p>Law-making, policy formulation, and legislative debates</p>\n<p>Role of committees, leadership, and parliamentary staff</p>\n<p>Transparency, public participation, and legislative ethics</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of parliamentary systems and governance models</p>\n<p>International standards, treaties, and best practices in legislative governance</p>\n<p>Cross-jurisdictional lessons for effective parliamentary law and procedure</p>\n<h4>4. Democracy, Human Rights, and Rule of Law</h4>\n<p>Strengthening democratic processes through effective legislative governance</p>\n<p>Protection of civil liberties, minority representation, and human rights in legislation</p>\n<p>Legal safeguards, judicial oversight, and constitutional compliance</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Technology, digital governance, and modern legislative tools</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, political science, public policy, and governance</p>\n<p>Policy recommendations, parliamentary reforms, and practical governance solutions</p>\n<p>IJPSL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of law and parliamentary studies, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to strengthen legislative governance, accountability, and democratic practices globally.</p>",
