        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Regional Trade Agreements and Law (IJRTAL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the legal, regulatory, and policy dimensions of regional trade agreements (RTAs) and international trade law. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, economists, policymakers, trade practitioners, and researchers to critically examine the formation, implementation, and impact of regional trade agreements on national and global economies.</p>\n<p>IJRTAL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, economics, and international relations, promoting evidence-based insights into trade regulation, dispute settlement, and policy harmonization. Contributions analyzing legal frameworks, comparative trade law, dispute resolution mechanisms, and the socio-economic implications of RTAs are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Legal Frameworks for Regional Trade Agreements</h4>\n<p>National and international legal provisions governing RTAs</p>\n<p>Treaty interpretation, compliance, and enforcement mechanisms</p>\n<p>Legal integration and harmonization across jurisdictions</p>\n<h4>2. Trade Policy and Economic Governance</h4>\n<p>Policy formulation and regulatory challenges in regional trade</p>\n<p>Impact of RTAs on domestic industries, competition, and investment</p>\n<p>Economic integration, tariff regulation, and market access</p>\n<h4>3. Dispute Resolution and Compliance</h4>\n<p>Legal mechanisms for dispute settlement in RTAs</p>\n<p>Arbitration, mediation, and judicial review of trade disputes</p>\n<p>Compliance monitoring and enforcement strategies</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of regional trade agreements across regions</p>\n<p>Interaction of RTAs with World Trade Organization (WTO) law</p>\n<p>Lessons from global and regional experiences in trade governance</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Technology, digital trade, and e-commerce in RTAs</p>\n<p>Environmental, social, and labor considerations in trade agreements</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, economics, policy, and international relations</p>\n<p>IJRTAL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines regional trade agreements and their legal, economic, and policy dimensions, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to enhance fair, effective, and sustainable trade governance worldwide.</p>",
