        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Maritime Law and Blue Economy (IJMLBE) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on maritime law, ocean governance, and sustainable utilization of marine resources. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, marine scientists, economists, and practitioners to critically examine the legal, regulatory, and policy frameworks governing maritime activities and the blue economy.</p>\n<p>IJMLBE seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, environmental science, economics, and policy, promoting evidence-based insights into maritime governance, sustainable resource management, and the socio-economic development of coastal and oceanic regions. Contributions analyzing maritime law, marine conservation, ocean governance, and blue economy strategies are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Maritime Law and Governance</h4>\n<p>International and national legal frameworks governing maritime activities</p>\n<p>Law of the sea, shipping regulation, and maritime security</p>\n<p>Ports, shipping contracts, and dispute resolution in maritime contexts</p>\n<h4>2. Blue Economy and Sustainable Development</h4>\n<p>Legal and policy frameworks for sustainable ocean resource use</p>\n<p>Fisheries management, marine biodiversity conservation, and renewable energy</p>\n<p>Coastal development, marine tourism, and economic sustainability</p>\n<h4>3. Environmental Protection and Ocean Governance</h4>\n<p>Marine pollution, environmental compliance, and conservation law</p>\n<p>Climate change impacts on maritime activities and coastal regions</p>\n<p>Integrated ocean governance and ecosystem-based management</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of maritime law and blue economy policies across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International treaties, conventions, and regional cooperation in maritime governance</p>\n<p>Lessons from global and regional practices in ocean management</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Technology, maritime innovation, and digital tools in ocean governance</p>\n<p>Socio-economic and legal implications of emerging maritime industries</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, economics, environmental science, and policy</p>\n<p>IJMLBE serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of maritime law and the blue economy, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to promote sustainable, equitable, and legally sound ocean governance worldwide.</p>",
