        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Aviation and Space Law (IJASL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the legal, regulatory, and policy dimensions of aviation and space activities. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, aerospace professionals, and researchers to critically examine national and international legal frameworks governing air and space law, regulatory compliance, and technological advancements in aviation and outer space.</p>\n<p>IJASL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, policy, science, and technology, promoting evidence-based insights into aviation governance, space exploration, liability, and the socio-economic and ethical implications of air and space activities. Contributions analyzing aviation law, space treaties, regulatory mechanisms, dispute resolution, and emerging challenges in aerospace governance are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Aviation Law and Governance</h4>\n<p>National and international legal frameworks for civil and commercial aviation</p>\n<p>Aviation safety, security, and regulatory compliance</p>\n<p>Air traffic management, liability, and dispute resolution in aviation</p>\n<h4>2. Space Law and Policy</h4>\n<p>Legal regimes governing outer space activities and exploration</p>\n<p>International treaties, conventions, and space governance frameworks</p>\n<p>Liability, property rights, and regulation of satellites and space technology</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of aviation and space law across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>Cross-border regulatory challenges and international cooperation</p>\n<p>Lessons from global practices in aerospace governance</p>\n<h4>4. Human Rights, Ethics, and Socio-Economic Implications</h4>\n<p>Ethical considerations in space exploration and aviation technology</p>\n<p>Access, equity, and the socio-economic impact of aviation and space activities</p>\n<p>Public safety, environmental protection, and human rights in aerospace operations</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Technological innovation, AI, and digitalization in aviation and space</p>\n<p>Environmental sustainability, space debris, and climate considerations</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, policy, engineering, and science</p>\n<p>IJASL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of aviation, space law, and policy, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to enhance safe, sustainable, and legally sound aerospace governance globally.</p>",
