        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Global Journal of Intellectual Property and Creative Industries Law (GJIP-CIL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on intellectual property (IP) law and its intersection with the creative industries. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, industry practitioners, and researchers to critically examine legal frameworks, policy developments, and regulatory challenges affecting intellectual property rights in creative sectors such as music, film, publishing, digital media, and design.</p>\n<p>GJIP-CIL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, economics, cultural studies, and policy, promoting evidence-based insights into the protection, management, and commercialization of creative works. Contributions analyzing IP law, copyright, trademark, patent, licensing, innovation policy, and the socio-economic implications of creative industries are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Intellectual Property Law</h4>\n<p>Copyright, trademark, patent, and trade secret law</p>\n<p>IP enforcement, licensing, and dispute resolution</p>\n<p>International treaties, conventions, and harmonization of IP law</p>\n<h4>2. Creative Industries Law and Policy</h4>\n<p>Legal and regulatory frameworks for music, film, publishing, and digital media</p>\n<p>Cultural industries, innovation policy, and creative entrepreneurship</p>\n<p>Protection and commercialization of creative works</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of IP law across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>Cross-border IP disputes, enforcement, and global policy approaches</p>\n<p>Lessons from international experiences in creative industry governance</p>\n<h4>4. Technology, Innovation, and Emerging Challenges</h4>\n<p>Digital technologies, AI, and IP law</p>\n<p>Challenges of IP protection in the digital economy</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, technology, and creative practice</p>\n<h4>5. Socio-Economic and Cultural Implications</h4>\n<p>Role of IP law in promoting innovation, creativity, and economic development</p>\n<p>Access to knowledge, public interest, and equity considerations</p>\n<p>Cultural policy, social justice, and the ethics of intellectual property</p>\n<p>GJIP-CIL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the legal, policy, and socio-economic dimensions of intellectual property and creative industries, fostering research, debate, and practical solutions to enhance innovation, creativity, and sustainable economic growth globally.</p>",
