        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of Sports Law and Policy (IJSLP) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the legal, regulatory, and policy aspects of sports at national and international levels. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, sports administrators, and researchers to critically examine laws, regulations, and policies that govern professional, amateur, and recreational sports.</p>\n<p>IJSLP seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, sports management, ethics, and public policy, promoting evidence-based insights into governance, dispute resolution, integrity, and the socio-economic impact of sports. Contributions analyzing sports law, policy development, compliance, athlete rights, and emerging challenges in sports governance are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Sports Law and Governance</h4>\n<p>Legal frameworks governing national and international sports</p>\n<p>Regulatory compliance, sports federations, and institutional governance</p>\n<p>Anti-doping laws, integrity, and dispute resolution mechanisms</p>\n<h4>2. Athlete Rights and Social Justice</h4>\n<p>Protection of athlete rights, contracts, and labor issues</p>\n<p>Gender equity, inclusion, and diversity in sports</p>\n<p>Ethical considerations, child protection, and social responsibility</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of sports law across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International sports treaties, conventions, and organizational regulations</p>\n<p>Lessons from global best practices in sports governance</p>\n<h4>4. Policy, Regulation, and Development</h4>\n<p>Sports policy formulation, implementation, and monitoring</p>\n<p>Sports development programs, infrastructure, and public participation</p>\n<p>Legal and policy approaches to professional, amateur, and grassroots sports</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Technology, digital media, and AI in sports regulation</p>\n<p>Sports commercialization, intellectual property, and broadcasting rights</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, policy, management, and social sciences</p>\n<p>IJSLP serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of law and sports policy, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to enhance governance, fairness, and development in sports worldwide.</p>",
