        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Global Journal of Taxation and Fiscal Law (GJTF) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on taxation, fiscal policy, and the legal frameworks governing public finance. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, economists, policymakers, and practitioners to critically examine national and international tax laws, fiscal governance, and regulatory mechanisms that influence revenue collection, economic policy, and public accountability.</p>\n<p>GJTF seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, economics, public policy, and finance, promoting evidence-based insights into tax compliance, fiscal reforms, and the socio-economic implications of taxation systems. Contributions analyzing tax law, fiscal policy, comparative taxation, dispute resolution, and emerging challenges in public finance are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Tax Law and Administration</h4>\n<p>National and international legal frameworks governing taxation</p>\n<p>Tax compliance, enforcement, and dispute resolution mechanisms</p>\n<p>Corporate taxation, income tax, VAT, and indirect taxation</p>\n<h4>2. Fiscal Policy and Governance</h4>\n<p>Public finance management, budgeting, and fiscal responsibility</p>\n<p>Legal and policy measures for revenue mobilization</p>\n<p>Accountability, transparency, and governance in fiscal matters</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of taxation laws and fiscal policies across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International tax treaties, transfer pricing, and cross-border taxation</p>\n<p>Lessons from global fiscal governance and best practices</p>\n<h4>4. Emerging Challenges and Innovation</h4>\n<p>Digital economy, e-commerce, and taxation</p>\n<p>Cryptocurrency, blockchain, and fintech implications for tax law</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, economics, and technology</p>\n<h4>5. Socio-Economic Implications and Public Policy</h4>\n<p>Equity, fairness, and social justice in taxation</p>\n<p>Impact of tax policy on economic development and public welfare</p>\n<p>Legal reforms and policy recommendations for sustainable fiscal governance</p>\n<p>GJTF serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines taxation and fiscal law, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to enhance legal certainty, financial governance, and socio-economic development globally.</p>",
