        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Evidence, Procedure and Justice (JEPJ) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on evidence law, procedural law, and the broader administration of justice. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, practitioners, judges, and policymakers to critically examine the legal frameworks, procedural norms, and evidentiary standards that underpin fair and effective judicial processes.</p>\n<p>JEPJ seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, criminology, forensic science, and public policy, promoting evidence-based insights into procedural justice, judicial decision-making, and the protection of rights within legal systems. Contributions analyzing evidence law, criminal and civil procedure, comparative legal systems, and reforms in judicial processes are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Evidence Law</h4>\n<p>Principles and standards of evidence in criminal and civil proceedings</p>\n<p>Admissibility, burden of proof, and evidentiary procedures</p>\n<p>Forensic evidence, digital evidence, and expert testimony</p>\n<h4>2. Procedural Law and Justice Administration</h4>\n<p>Civil and criminal procedural rules and their implementation</p>\n<p>Court procedures, case management, and judicial efficiency</p>\n<p>Procedural safeguards, due process, and access to justice</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of evidentiary and procedural systems across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International legal standards and best practices</p>\n<p>Harmonization of procedural rules in cross-border disputes</p>\n<h4>4. Human Rights, Fair Trial, and Ethical Considerations</h4>\n<p>Protection of defendants’, victims’, and witnesses’ rights</p>\n<p>Fair trial standards, judicial accountability, and transparency</p>\n<p>Ethical considerations in legal practice and judicial decision-making</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Technology, digital evidence, AI, and automation in judicial processes</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, criminology, and public policy</p>\n<p>Innovations and reforms to enhance efficiency, fairness, and access to justice</p>\n<p>JEPJ serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the law of evidence, procedural rules, and the administration of justice, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to promote fair, transparent, and effective judicial systems worldwide.</p>",
