        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of International Investment and Arbitration Law (JIIAL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on international investment law, dispute resolution, and arbitration. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, practitioners, policymakers, and arbitrators to critically examine national and international legal frameworks governing foreign investment, investment treaties, and arbitration proceedings.</p>\n<p>JIIAL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, economics, international relations, and policy analysis, promoting evidence-based insights into investment protection, dispute settlement, and the governance of international economic relations. Contributions analyzing investment treaties, arbitration procedures, enforcement of awards, and emerging challenges in international investment law are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. International Investment Law</h4>\n<p>Bilateral and multilateral investment treaties</p>\n<p>Legal frameworks for foreign direct investment (FDI)</p>\n<p>Investor-state dispute settlement (ISDS) mechanisms</p>\n<h4>2. Arbitration and Dispute Resolution</h4>\n<p>International commercial and investment arbitration procedures</p>\n<p>Enforcement of arbitral awards and compliance mechanisms</p>\n<p>Procedural innovations, ethics, and best practices in arbitration</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of investment law and arbitration frameworks across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>Regional and global investment agreements</p>\n<p>Lessons from international arbitration practice and case law</p>\n<h4>4. Policy, Governance, and Economic Implications</h4>\n<p>Role of investment law in promoting economic development</p>\n<p>State sovereignty, regulatory powers, and investor protections</p>\n<p>Policy implications of arbitration outcomes on domestic law and governance</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Technology, digital assets, and investment arbitration</p>\n<p>Sustainable investment, human rights, and environmental considerations</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, economics, and international relations</p>\n<p>JIIAL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines international investment and arbitration law, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to enhance legal certainty, effective dispute resolution, and sustainable economic governance globally.</p>",
