        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Law and Rural Development (JLRD) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the legal, policy, and socio-economic aspects of rural development. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, development practitioners, and researchers to critically examine how law and governance shape rural livelihoods, resource management, and socio-economic transformation.</p>\n<p>JLRD seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, rural development studies, public policy, and social sciences, promoting evidence-based insights into land governance, rural infrastructure, agricultural law, and inclusive development strategies. Contributions analyzing rural legal frameworks, policy interventions, community rights, and comparative rural development practices are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Rural Law and Governance</h4>\n<p>Land tenure, property rights, and agricultural legislation</p>\n<p>Legal frameworks governing rural institutions, cooperatives, and local governance</p>\n<p>Regulatory compliance, dispute resolution, and institutional accountability</p>\n<h4>2. Rural Development Policy and Practice</h4>\n<p>Policy frameworks for sustainable rural livelihoods, poverty alleviation, and economic development</p>\n<p>Legal aspects of rural infrastructure, water resources, and energy access</p>\n<p>Social protection, microfinance, and community development initiatives</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of rural development law across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International treaties, conventions, and rural development programs</p>\n<p>Lessons from global best practices in rural legal and policy governance</p>\n<h4>4. Human Rights, Social Justice, and Equity</h4>\n<p>Rights of rural communities, women, and marginalized groups</p>\n<p>Access to justice, legal aid, and participatory governance</p>\n<p>Balancing development objectives with social and environmental justice</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Climate change, environmental law, and sustainable rural development</p>\n<p>Technology, digital inclusion, and innovation in rural governance</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, policy, economics, and social sciences</p>\n<p>JLRD serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of law and rural development, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to promote inclusive, equitable, and sustainable rural transformation worldwide.</p>",
