        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Refugee Protection and Statelessness Law (JRFPSL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the legal, policy, and human rights dimensions of refugee protection, statelessness, and forced migration. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, human rights practitioners, policymakers, and researchers to critically examine international, regional, and national frameworks addressing the protection of refugees and stateless persons.</p>\n<p>JRFPSL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, human rights, international relations, and social sciences, promoting evidence-based insights into asylum law, refugee rights, statelessness prevention, and policy interventions. Contributions analyzing legal protections, comparative refugee and statelessness frameworks, displacement crises, and innovative solutions for vulnerable populations are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Refugee Law and Protection</h4>\n<p>International legal frameworks, including the 1951 Refugee Convention and regional instruments</p>\n<p>National asylum procedures, refugee status determination, and rights protection</p>\n<p>Humanitarian law, protection mechanisms, and refugee integration</p>\n<h4>2. Statelessness and Legal Identity</h4>\n<p>Causes and consequences of statelessness</p>\n<p>Nationality law, legal remedies, and documentation challenges</p>\n<p>International frameworks for the prevention and reduction of statelessness</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of refugee and statelessness law across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International cooperation, treaties, and regional approaches</p>\n<p>Lessons from global practices in displacement management and legal protection</p>\n<h4>4. Human Rights, Social Justice, and Policy Implications</h4>\n<p>Protection of vulnerable groups, including women, children, and minorities</p>\n<p>Access to justice, social services, and legal aid for displaced populations</p>\n<p>Balancing state sovereignty, security, and human rights obligations</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Climate-induced displacement, migration crises, and humanitarian emergencies</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, policy, sociology, and human rights advocacy</p>\n<p>Innovative legal, policy, and technological solutions for refugee and stateless populations</p>\n<p>JRFPSL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of law, refugee protection, and statelessness, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to enhance legal protection, social justice, and human rights worldwide.</p>",
