        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Children’s Rights and Juvenile Justice (JCRJJ) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the legal, social, and policy dimensions of children’s rights and juvenile justice systems. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, child rights advocates, policymakers, and practitioners to critically examine national and international frameworks that protect the rights of children and ensure fair and effective juvenile justice.</p>\n<p>JCRJJ seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, social work, psychology, and public policy, promoting evidence-based insights into child protection, juvenile justice procedures, and the broader socio-legal context affecting children. Contributions analyzing legal safeguards, juvenile justice reforms, children’s rights implementation, and comparative practices are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Children’s Rights Law</h4>\n<p>International and national legal frameworks protecting children (e.g., UNCRC)</p>\n<p>Rights to education, health, protection from abuse and exploitation</p>\n<p>Legal mechanisms for safeguarding vulnerable children</p>\n<h4>2. Juvenile Justice Systems</h4>\n<p>Procedural safeguards for children in conflict with the law</p>\n<p>Juvenile courts, rehabilitation programs, and restorative justice approaches</p>\n<p>Sentencing, diversion, and alternatives to incarceration</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of juvenile justice systems across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International treaties, regional conventions, and policy standards</p>\n<p>Lessons from global best practices in child protection and juvenile justice</p>\n<h4>4. Social Justice, Ethics, and Policy Implications</h4>\n<p>Child welfare, social inclusion, and equitable access to justice</p>\n<p>Ethical considerations in handling child-related cases</p>\n<p>Policy reforms, advocacy, and implementation challenges</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Technology, digital media, and the protection of children online</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, social sciences, psychology, and public policy</p>\n<p>Innovative solutions for enhancing children’s rights and juvenile justice systems</p>\n<p>JCRJJ serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of children’s rights and juvenile justice, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to promote protection, fairness, and social justice for children worldwide.</p>",
