        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Global Journal of Intellectual Property Law, Innovation, and Societal Impact (GJIP-ISI) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on intellectual property (IP) law, innovation policy, and the societal implications of creative and technological developments. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, industry practitioners, and researchers to critically examine how IP frameworks influence innovation, economic development, and social transformation.</p>\n<p>GJIP-ISI seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, economics, technology, and social sciences, promoting evidence-based insights into intellectual property protection, innovation management, and the broader societal consequences of IP-driven developments. Contributions analyzing IP law, policy reforms, innovation ecosystems, and socio-economic impacts are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Intellectual Property Law</h4>\n<p>Legal frameworks governing patents, copyrights, trademarks, and trade secrets</p>\n<p>Enforcement, licensing, and dispute resolution in IP law</p>\n<p>International treaties, conventions, and harmonization of IP regulations</p>\n<h4>2. Innovation and Technology</h4>\n<p>Role of IP in promoting technological and creative innovation</p>\n<p>Management of IP assets, commercialization, and technology transfer</p>\n<p>Emerging technologies, AI, and digital innovation implications</p>\n<h4>3. Societal and Economic Impact</h4>\n<p>Socio-economic effects of IP law on industries, markets, and communities</p>\n<p>Access to knowledge, public interest, and social equity considerations</p>\n<p>Policy interventions to balance innovation incentives with societal benefits</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of IP law and innovation policy across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International cooperation, treaties, and cross-border IP enforcement</p>\n<p>Lessons from global best practices in IP governance and innovation management</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Challenges of IP protection in the digital economy</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, technology, economics, and social sciences</p>\n<p>Innovative strategies to align IP law with sustainable and inclusive societal development</p>\n<p>GJIP-ISI serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of intellectual property law, innovation, and societal impact, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to enhance innovation, equity, and sustainable development worldwide.</p>",
