        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Global Journal of Labor Law, Industrial Relations, and Organizational Studies (GJLL-IROS) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on labor law, industrial relations, and organizational governance. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, labor practitioners, and organizational researchers to critically examine the legal, regulatory, and socio-economic frameworks shaping labor markets, workplace relations, and organizational practices.</p>\n<p>GJLL-IROS seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, management studies, economics, and social sciences, promoting evidence-based insights into labor rights, employment policy, industrial disputes, and organizational governance. Contributions analyzing labor law, industrial relations, workplace reforms, and comparative employment practices are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Labor Law and Employment Regulation</h4>\n<p>National and international labor legislation and compliance</p>\n<p>Workers’ rights, employment contracts, and workplace safety</p>\n<p>Dispute resolution, collective bargaining, and legal remedies</p>\n<h4>2. Industrial Relations and Workplace Governance</h4>\n<p>Employer-employee relations, trade unions, and negotiation frameworks</p>\n<p>Labor market dynamics, industrial disputes, and conflict management</p>\n<p>Organizational policies, HR governance, and labor standards</p>\n<h4>3. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of labor law and industrial relations across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International labor standards, conventions, and best practices</p>\n<p>Cross-border employment law and global workforce management</p>\n<h4>4. Organizational Studies and Management Implications</h4>\n<p>Organizational behavior, management practices, and labor productivity</p>\n<p>Ethical governance, workplace diversity, and inclusion policies</p>\n<p>HR innovation, digitalization, and workforce development</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Impact of technology, AI, and automation on labor markets</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, management, economics, and social sciences</p>\n<p>Policy innovation for fair, sustainable, and resilient workplace practices</p>\n<p>GJLL-IROS serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines labor law, industrial relations, and organizational studies, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to enhance equitable, efficient, and sustainable work environments worldwide.</p>",
