        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of AI, Robotics and Law (IJARL) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on the legal, ethical, and regulatory dimensions of artificial intelligence (AI) and robotics. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, technologists, policymakers, and researchers to critically examine national and international frameworks governing AI systems, robotics technologies, and their societal implications.</p>\n<p>IJARL seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, computer science, engineering, and ethics, promoting evidence-based insights into regulation, governance, accountability, and the societal impact of AI and robotic technologies. Contributions analyzing legal challenges, policy frameworks, ethical dilemmas, and comparative perspectives are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. AI and Robotics Law</h4>\n<p>Legal frameworks for the design, deployment, and use of AI systems and robotics</p>\n<p>Liability, accountability, and risk management for autonomous technologies</p>\n<p>Intellectual property, data protection, and compliance issues</p>\n<h4>2. Ethical and Societal Implications</h4>\n<p>Ethical frameworks for AI and robotics deployment</p>\n<p>Bias, fairness, transparency, and human rights considerations</p>\n<p>Societal impact, public trust, and social acceptance of emerging technologies</p>\n<h4>3. Policy and Governance</h4>\n<p>National and international regulatory approaches to AI and robotics</p>\n<p>Policy development for innovation, safety, and responsible AI</p>\n<p>Standards, certification, and governance mechanisms</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of AI and robotics law across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>International treaties, guidelines, and harmonization efforts</p>\n<p>Lessons from global best practices in regulation and governance</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>AI-driven automation, autonomous vehicles, drones, and robotics applications</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, technology, ethics, and social sciences</p>\n<p>Innovative strategies for legal, ethical, and policy frameworks for AI and robotics</p>\n<p>IJARL serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of AI, robotics, and law, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to advance responsible innovation, legal certainty, and societal benefit worldwide.</p>",
