        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Journal of International Law, Peace Studies, and Conflict Mitigation (IJIL-PSCM) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on international law, peacebuilding, and conflict mitigation strategies. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, diplomats, and researchers to critically examine international legal frameworks, normative principles, and practical strategies for preventing, managing, and resolving conflicts.</p>\n<p>IJIL-PSCM seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, international relations, political science, and peace studies, promoting evidence-based insights into conflict resolution, humanitarian protection, and global governance. Contributions analyzing treaties, international dispute settlement, peacebuilding mechanisms, and policy innovation are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. International Law and Global Governance</h4>\n<p>Legal frameworks governing conflict prevention, resolution, and humanitarian intervention</p>\n<p>International treaties, conventions, and customary law</p>\n<p>Compliance, enforcement, and the role of international courts and tribunals</p>\n<h4>2. Peace Studies and Conflict Resolution</h4>\n<p>Theories and practices of peacebuilding, negotiation, and mediation</p>\n<p>Post-conflict reconstruction, reconciliation, and transitional justice</p>\n<p>Role of local communities, NGOs, and international organizations in sustaining peace</p>\n<h4>3. Conflict Mitigation and Security Policy</h4>\n<p>Preventive diplomacy, early warning systems, and crisis management</p>\n<p>National and regional security arrangements</p>\n<p>Policy frameworks for mitigating social, political, and economic conflict</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and Regional Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of conflict resolution and peacebuilding frameworks across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>Lessons from regional and international best practices</p>\n<p>Cross-border cooperation and collaborative dispute management</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Climate-induced conflict, migration, and resource disputes</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, political science, sociology, and ethics</p>\n<p>Innovative strategies for legal, policy, and practical approaches to peace and conflict mitigation</p>\n<p>IJIL-PSCM serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of international law, peace studies, and conflict mitigation, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to strengthen global peace, justice, and governance.</p>",
