        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The International Review of Security Policy, International Law, and Peace Studies (IR-SPILPS) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on security policy, international law, and peace studies. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, diplomats, and researchers to critically examine the frameworks, strategies, and normative principles that govern global security, conflict management, and peacebuilding.</p>\n<p>IR-SPILPS seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, political science, international relations, and peace studies, promoting evidence-based insights into security governance, legal compliance, and sustainable peace initiatives. Contributions analyzing national and international security policies, legal frameworks, conflict resolution, and peace strategies are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Security Policy and Governance</h4>\n<p>National and international security strategies and policy frameworks</p>\n<p>Counter-terrorism, defense policy, and intelligence governance</p>\n<p>Risk assessment, crisis management, and strategic planning</p>\n<h4>2. International Law and Legal Frameworks</h4>\n<p>Legal principles governing armed conflict, peacekeeping, and humanitarian intervention</p>\n<p>Treaties, conventions, and customary international law</p>\n<p>Compliance, enforcement, and accountability mechanisms</p>\n<h4>3. Peace Studies and Conflict Resolution</h4>\n<p>Theories and practices of peacebuilding, mediation, and reconciliation</p>\n<p>Post-conflict reconstruction, transitional justice, and humanitarian protection</p>\n<p>Role of international organizations, NGOs, and local communities in sustaining peace</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and Regional Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of security policy, law, and peace initiatives across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>Regional security arrangements and cross-border collaboration</p>\n<p>Lessons from global best practices in conflict mitigation and governance</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Climate security, cyber threats, migration, and resource conflicts</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, political science, sociology, and ethics</p>\n<p>Innovative strategies for enhancing security, legal compliance, and sustainable peace</p>\n<p>IR-SPILPS serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of security policy, international law, and peace studies, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to strengthen global security, governance, and conflict resolution.</p>",
