        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Criminal Justice Ethics, Forensic Policy, and Societal Impact (JCJ-EFPSI) is a peer-reviewed academic journal published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, dedicated to advancing interdisciplinary research on criminal justice ethics, forensic policy, and the broader societal implications of law enforcement and legal systems. The journal provides a platform for scholars, practitioners, policymakers, and social scientists to critically examine ethical standards, policy frameworks, and social outcomes within criminal justice systems globally.</p>\n<p>JCJ-EFPSI seeks to foster research that integrates legal analysis, ethical inquiry, and policy evaluation to promote justice, accountability, and societal well-being. Contributions that explore forensic science, criminal law ethics, policy reform, and the social impact of criminal justice practices are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, policy analyses, theoretical essays, and interdisciplinary reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<ul><li>Criminal Justice Ethics</li><li>Ethical frameworks in law enforcement, prosecution, and judicial decision-making</li><li>Professional accountability, integrity, and human rights considerations</li><li>Ethical challenges in emerging criminal justice technologies</li><li>Forensic Policy and Practice</li><li>Forensic science policy, regulation, and best practices</li><li>Evidence collection, analysis, and technological integration in criminal investigations</li><li>Policy evaluation and reform for efficient and ethical forensic practices</li><li>Societal Impact of Criminal Justice</li><li>Social, cultural, and economic implications of criminal law enforcement</li><li>Community relations, restorative justice, and rehabilitation strategies</li><li>Policy approaches to reduce systemic inequality and enhance public trust</li><li>Interdisciplinary and Comparative Research</li><li>Integration of law, criminology, sociology, psychology, and public policy</li><li>Comparative studies of criminal justice ethics, forensic policies, and societal outcomes</li><li>Emerging trends in criminal justice reform, ethical governance, and technology in policing</li><li>JCJ-EFPSI serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines criminal justice ethics, promotes sound forensic policy, and advances societal impact analysis, contributing to accountable, equitable, and forward-looking justice systems worldwide.</li></ul>",
