        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of International Humanitarian Law, Peacebuilding, and Conflict Mediation (J-IHLPCM) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on international humanitarian law, strategies for peacebuilding, and conflict mediation practices. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, policymakers, practitioners, and researchers to critically examine the legal, ethical, and practical frameworks that govern humanitarian protection, conflict resolution, and sustainable peace initiatives worldwide.</p>\n<p>J-IHLPCM seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, international relations, political science, and peace studies, promoting evidence-based insights into humanitarian protection, conflict prevention, and mediation strategies. Contributions analyzing international legal frameworks, peacebuilding programs, and innovative approaches to conflict resolution are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. International Humanitarian Law</h4>\n<p>Legal principles governing armed conflict, protection of civilians, and humanitarian interventions</p>\n<p>Treaties, conventions, and customary international law</p>\n<p>Compliance, enforcement, and accountability mechanisms</p>\n<h4>2. Peacebuilding Strategies</h4>\n<p>Theories and practices of reconciliation, post-conflict reconstruction, and transitional justice</p>\n<p>Role of local communities, NGOs, and international organizations in sustaining peace</p>\n<p>Strategies for social cohesion, institutional rebuilding, and conflict prevention</p>\n<h4>3. Conflict Mediation and Resolution</h4>\n<p>Negotiation, diplomacy, and third-party mediation approaches</p>\n<p>Early warning systems and preventive measures for conflict mitigation</p>\n<p>Comparative and innovative methods for dispute resolution in domestic and international contexts</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of humanitarian law, peacebuilding, and mediation frameworks across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>Lessons from regional and global experiences in conflict management</p>\n<p>Cross-border cooperation and collaborative governance in peace initiatives</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Climate-induced conflicts, migration crises, and resource disputes</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, political science, sociology, and ethics</p>\n<p>Innovative approaches to enhancing legal, policy, and practical frameworks for peace and conflict mediation</p>\n<p>J-IHLPCM serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of international humanitarian law, peacebuilding, and conflict mediation, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to advance justice, security, and sustainable peace worldwide.</p>",
