        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of International Trade Law, Economic Development, and Legal Innovation (JITLED-LI) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on international trade law, its impact on economic development, and innovative legal frameworks. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, economists, policymakers, and researchers to critically examine trade regulations, economic governance, and the evolving role of law in facilitating sustainable and inclusive development.</p>\n<p>JITLED-LI seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, economics, policy studies, and international relations, promoting evidence-based insights into trade regulation, economic reform, and legal innovation. Contributions analyzing international trade agreements, legal reforms, economic policy, and comparative legal frameworks are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. International Trade Law</h4>\n<p>WTO regulations, bilateral and multilateral trade agreements</p>\n<p>Trade dispute resolution and arbitration mechanisms</p>\n<p>Regulatory compliance, customs law, and cross-border trade governance</p>\n<h4>2. Economic Development and Policy</h4>\n<p>Legal frameworks supporting economic growth, investment, and industrialization</p>\n<p>Trade facilitation, market access, and economic integration strategies</p>\n<p>Policy measures promoting equitable and sustainable development</p>\n<h4>3. Legal Innovation and Governance</h4>\n<p>Innovative legal instruments for trade and economic regulation</p>\n<p>Digital trade, e-commerce law, and emerging technologies in trade law</p>\n<p>Reforming legal frameworks to address global economic challenges</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of trade law and economic governance across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>Lessons from international best practices in trade regulation and economic development</p>\n<p>Cross-border legal and policy harmonization initiatives</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Impact of climate change, digitalization, and geopolitical shifts on trade law</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, economics, international relations, and public policy</p>\n<p>Innovative strategies for legal and policy adaptation to global trade and development dynamics</p>\n<p>JITLED-LI serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of international trade law, economic development, and legal innovation, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to advance fair, sustainable, and effective trade governance worldwide.</p>",
