        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Interplanetary Law, Technological Diplomacy, and Global Futures (JIL-TDGF) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on space law, emerging technologies, and their governance in the context of interplanetary exploration and global diplomacy. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, scientists, policymakers, and international relations experts to critically examine legal frameworks, diplomatic strategies, and policy innovations governing outer space, technological development, and humanity’s future in space exploration.</p>\n<p>JIL-TDGF seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, technology, space policy, and international diplomacy, promoting evidence-based insights into the legal, ethical, and strategic challenges of interplanetary exploration. Contributions analyzing space law, technological governance, diplomatic negotiations, and future-oriented policy frameworks are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Interplanetary and Space Law</h4>\n<p>International and national legal frameworks for outer space exploration</p>\n<p>Space treaties, conventions, and customary law</p>\n<p>Liability, resource rights, and regulatory compliance in space activities</p>\n<h4>2. Technological Diplomacy and Governance</h4>\n<p>Global governance of emerging technologies related to space exploration</p>\n<p>International cooperation, negotiation, and diplomacy in technological development</p>\n<p>Policy frameworks for collaborative space missions and innovation management</p>\n<h4>3. Ethical, Social, and Strategic Implications</h4>\n<p>Ethical considerations in space exploration and technological advancement</p>\n<p>Societal impacts of interplanetary exploration and technological innovation</p>\n<p>Strategic security and risk management in outer space operations</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of space law, technology policy, and diplomatic frameworks</p>\n<p>Lessons from international best practices in space governance and technology diplomacy</p>\n<p>Cross-border collaboration and global policy harmonization for space futures</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Planetary resource management, space sustainability, and environmental ethics</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, engineering, international relations, and ethics</p>\n<p>Innovative strategies for shaping legal, policy, and diplomatic frameworks for humanity’s future in space</p>\n<p>JIL-TDGF serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of interplanetary law, technological diplomacy, and global futures, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to advance responsible governance, innovation, and sustainable exploration beyond Earth.</p>",
