        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Medical Law and Public Health Policy (JML-PHP) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on medical law, health policy, and the regulation of public health systems. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, healthcare professionals, policymakers, and researchers to critically examine the legal, ethical, and policy frameworks governing healthcare delivery, public health initiatives, and medical governance.</p>\n<p>JML-PHP seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, public health, medical ethics, and policy studies, promoting evidence-based insights into health law, regulatory compliance, and health policy innovation. Contributions analyzing healthcare legislation, bioethics, public health governance, and comparative legal frameworks are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Medical Law and Legal Governance</h4>\n<p>National and international legal frameworks regulating medical practice</p>\n<p>Patient rights, medical negligence, and professional accountability</p>\n<p>Health regulation, licensing, and compliance mechanisms</p>\n<h4>2. Public Health Policy and Governance</h4>\n<p>Health policy design, implementation, and evaluation</p>\n<p>Disease prevention, vaccination programs, and emergency preparedness</p>\n<p>Governance of healthcare systems, equity, and access to care</p>\n<h4>3. Bioethics and Ethical Considerations</h4>\n<p>Ethical issues in medical practice, research, and healthcare delivery</p>\n<p>End-of-life decisions, informed consent, and patient autonomy</p>\n<p>Ethical implications of emerging medical technologies and AI in healthcare</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of medical law and public health policy across jurisdictions</p>\n<p>Lessons from global health governance, treaties, and collaborative frameworks</p>\n<p>Cross-border healthcare regulation and international health law compliance</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Pandemic preparedness, health emergencies, and legal responses</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, medicine, sociology, and public policy</p>\n<p>Innovative strategies for equitable, ethical, and efficient healthcare systems</p>\n<p>JML-PHP serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of medical law and public health policy, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to strengthen health governance, ethical medical practice, and population well-being worldwide.</p>",
