        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Poverty, Inequality, and Economic Justice (JP-IEJ) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on poverty alleviation, economic inequality, and social justice. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, economists, policymakers, and social scientists to critically examine the legal, economic, and policy mechanisms that shape equitable development, social welfare, and economic justice globally.</p>\n<p>JP-IEJ seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, economics, sociology, and public policy, promoting evidence-based insights into strategies for reducing poverty, addressing structural inequalities, and enhancing social and economic rights. Contributions analyzing legal reforms, social policy innovation, and comparative approaches to economic justice are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Poverty Alleviation and Social Policy</h4>\n<p>Legal and policy frameworks for poverty reduction</p>\n<p>Social welfare programs, social protection, and economic inclusion strategies</p>\n<p>Community-based interventions and grassroots development initiatives</p>\n<h4>2. Economic Inequality and Justice</h4>\n<p>Structural inequality, wealth distribution, and labor market disparities</p>\n<p>Legal, economic, and policy mechanisms for promoting equity</p>\n<p>Comparative studies of taxation, social policy, and redistribution mechanisms</p>\n<h4>3. Rights-Based and Ethical Approaches</h4>\n<p>Economic and social rights, human rights frameworks, and ethical governance</p>\n<p>Legal strategies to address marginalization, discrimination, and exclusion</p>\n<p>Social justice-oriented policy analysis and implementation</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Comparative studies of poverty reduction and economic justice frameworks</p>\n<p>International treaties, development programs, and cross-border policy initiatives</p>\n<p>Lessons from global best practices in equitable economic governance</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Impact of globalization, climate change, and technological change on poverty and inequality</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, economics, sociology, and public policy</p>\n<p>Innovative strategies for sustainable, inclusive, and just economic systems</p>\n<p>JP-IEJ serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of poverty, inequality, and economic justice, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to promote equitable development, social inclusion, and human well-being worldwide.</p>",
