        "Aims & Scope": "<p>The Journal of Alternative Dispute Resolution and Mediation (JADR-M) is a peer-reviewed academic journal dedicated to advancing scholarship on alternative dispute resolution (ADR), mediation, and conflict management practices. Published by Academic Research Centre Journals Publishers, the journal provides a platform for legal scholars, practitioners, mediators, policymakers, and researchers to critically examine the legal, ethical, and practical frameworks that support effective conflict resolution in civil, commercial, and community contexts.</p>\n<p>JADR-M seeks to foster interdisciplinary research that integrates law, social sciences, organizational studies, and public policy, promoting evidence-based insights into dispute resolution mechanisms, mediation strategies, and the broader social, economic, and legal impact of ADR. Contributions analyzing ADR frameworks, mediation practice, negotiation techniques, and comparative approaches are particularly encouraged.</p>\n<h4>Scope</h4>\n<p><strong>The journal publishes original research articles, case studies, theoretical essays, comparative analyses, and policy reviews in areas including, but not limited to:</strong></p>\n<h4>1. Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) Mechanisms</h4>\n<p>Mediation, arbitration, negotiation, and conciliation processes</p>\n<p>Institutional frameworks and regulatory compliance in ADR</p>\n<p>Effectiveness, efficiency, and access to justice through ADR</p>\n<h4>2. Mediation Practice and Theory</h4>\n<p>Professional standards, ethical considerations, and training for mediators</p>\n<p>Conflict assessment, dispute analysis, and resolution strategies</p>\n<p>Innovative and hybrid mediation techniques</p>\n<h4>3. Legal and Policy Frameworks</h4>\n<p>National and international laws supporting ADR and mediation</p>\n<p>Policy development for dispute resolution in civil, commercial, and community sectors</p>\n<p>Comparative analysis of ADR systems across jurisdictions</p>\n<h4>4. Comparative and International Perspectives</h4>\n<p>Cross-border dispute resolution and international arbitration</p>\n<p>Lessons from global best practices in ADR and mediation</p>\n<p>Harmonization of legal frameworks for international conflict resolution</p>\n<h4>5. Emerging Challenges and Interdisciplinary Approaches</h4>\n<p>Technology-driven mediation and online dispute resolution (ODR)</p>\n<p>Interdisciplinary research linking law, social sciences, business, and ethics</p>\n<p>Innovative strategies for equitable, efficient, and culturally responsive dispute resolution</p>\n<p>JADR-M serves as a leading forum for scholarship that critically examines the intersection of alternative dispute resolution, mediation, and conflict management, fostering research, debate, and practical insights to enhance access to justice, social harmony, and effective conflict resolution worldwide.</p>",
